    ("Ampharos", "Light Pokémon", "Electric", "", "The bright light on its tail can be seen far away. It has been treasured since ancient times as a beacon."),
    ("Bellossom", "Flower Pokémon", "Grass", "", "Plentiful in the tropics. When it dances, its petals rub together and make a pleasant ringing sound."),
    ("Marill", "Aqua Mouse Pokémon", "Water", "Fairy", "The end of its tail serves as a buoy that keeps it from drowning, even in a vicious current."),
    ("Azumarill", "Aqua Rabbit Pokémon", "Water", "Fairy", "When it plays in water, it rolls up its elongated ears to prevent their insides from getting wet."),
    ("Sudowoodo", "Imitation Pokémon", "Rock", "", "It disguises itself as a tree to avoid attack. It hates water, so it will disappear if it starts raining."),
    ("Politoed", "Frog Pokémon", "Water", "", "Whenever three or more of these get together, they sing in a loud voice that sounds like bellowing."),
    ("Hoppip", "Cottonweed Pokémon", "Grass", "Flying", "Its body is so light, it must grip the ground firmly with its feet to keep from being blown away."),
    ("Skiploom", "Cottonweed Pokémon", "Grass", "Flying", "It spreads its petals to absorb sunlight. It also floats in the air to get closer to the sun."),
    ("Jumpluff", "Cottonweed Pokémon", "Grass", "Flying", "It drifts on seasonal winds and spreads its cotton-like spores all over the world to make more offspring."),
    ("Aipom", "Long Tail Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It lives atop tall trees. When leaping from branch to branch, it deftly uses its tail for balance."),
    ("Sunkern", "Seed Pokémon", "Grass", "", "It lives by drinking only dewdrops from under the leaves of plants. It is said that it eats nothing else."),
    ("Sunflora", "Sun Pokémon", "Grass", "", "In the daytime, it rushes about in a hectic manner, but it comes to a complete stop when the sun sets."),
    ("Yanma", "Clear Wing Pokémon", "Bug", "Flying", "Its large eyes can scan 360 degrees. It looks in all directions to seek out insects as its prey."),
    ("Wooper", "Water Fish Pokémon", "Water", "Ground", "When it walks around on the ground, it coats its body with a slimy, poisonous film."),
    ("Quagsire", "Water Fish Pokémon", "Water", "Ground", "Due to its relaxed and carefree attitude, it often bumps its head on boulders and boat hulls as it swims."),
    ("Espeon", "Sun Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "By reading air currents, it can predict things such as the weather or its foe’s next move."),
    ("Umbreon", "Moonlight Pokémon", "Dark", "", "When darkness falls, the rings on its body begin to glow, striking fear in the hearts of anyone nearby."),
    ("Murkrow", "Darkness Pokémon", "Dark", "Flying", "It is said that when chased, it lures its attacker onto dark mountain trails where the foe will get lost."),
    ("Slowking", "Royal Pokémon", "Water", "Psychic", "When its head was bitten, toxins entered Slowpoke’s head and unlocked an extraordinary power."),
    ("Misdreavus", "Screech Pokémon", "Ghost", "", "It loves to bite and yank people’s hair from behind without warning, just to see their shocked reactions."),
    ("Unown", "Symbol Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "Its flat, thin body is always stuck on walls. Its shape appears to have some meaning."),
    ("Wobbuffet", "Patient Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "To keep its pitch-black tail hidden, it lives quietly in the darkness. It is never first to attack."),
    ("Girafarig", "Long Neck Pokémon", "Normal", "Psychic", "Its tail, which also contains a small brain, may bite on its own if it notices an alluring smell."),
    ("Pineco", "Bagworm Pokémon", "Bug", "", "It hangs and waits for flying-insect prey to come near. It does not move about much on its own."),
    ("Forretress", "Bagworm Pokémon", "Bug", "Steel", "It remains immovably rooted to its tree. It scatters pieces of its hard shell to drive its enemies away."),
    ("Dunsparce", "Land Snake Pokémon", "Normal", "", "If spotted, it escapes by burrowing with its tail. It can hover just slightly using its wings."),
    ("Gligar", "Fly Scorpion Pokémon", "Ground", "Flying", "It usually clings to cliffs. When it spots its prey, it spreads its wings and glides down to attack."),
    ("Steelix", "Iron Snake Pokémon", "Steel", "Ground", "It is said that if an Onix lives for over 100 years, its composition changes to become diamond-like."),
    ("Snubbull", "Fairy Pokémon", "Fairy", "", "It has an active, playful nature. Many women like to frolic with it because of its affectionate ways."),
    ("Granbull", "Fairy Pokémon", "Fairy", "", "Because its fangs are too heavy, it always keeps its head tilted down. However, its Bite is powerful."),
    ("Qwilfish", "Balloon Pokémon", "Water", "Poison", "The small spikes covering its body developed from scales. They inject a toxin that causes fainting."),
    ("Scizor", "Pincer Pokémon", "Bug", "Steel", "Its wings are not used for flying. They are flapped at high speed to adjust its body temperature."),
    ("Shuckle", "Mold Pokémon", "Bug", "Rock", "It stores Berries inside its shell. To avoid attacks, it hides beneath rocks and remains completely still."),
    ("Heracross", "Single Horn Pokémon", "Bug", "Fighting", "Usually docile, but if disturbed while sipping honey, it chases off the intruder with its horn."),
    ("Sneasel", "Sharp Claw Pokémon", "Dark", "Ice", "Vicious in nature, it drives Pidgey from their nests and feasts on the eggs that are left behind."),
    ("Teddiursa", "Little Bear Pokémon", "Normal", "", "Before food becomes scarce in wintertime, its habit is to hoard food in many hidden locations."),
    ("Ursaring", "Hibernator Pokémon", "Normal", "", "With its ability to distinguish any smell, it unfailingly finds all food buried deep underground."),
    ("Slugma", "Lava Pokémon", "Fire", "", "A common sight in volcanic areas, it slowly slithers around in a constant search for warm places."),
    ("Magcargo", "Lava Pokémon", "Fire", "Rock", "Its brittle shell occasionally spouts intense flames that circulate throughout its body."),
    ("Swinub", "Pig Pokémon", "Ice", "Ground", "If it smells something enticing, it dashes off headlong to find the source of the aroma."),
    ("Piloswine", "Swine Pokémon", "Ice", "Ground", "If it charges at an enemy, the hairs on its back stand up straight. It is very sensitive to sound."),
    ("Corsola", "Coral Pokémon", "Water", "Rock", "In a south sea nation, the people live in communities that are built on groups of these Pokémon."),
    ("Remoraid", "Jet Pokémon", "Water", "", "Using its dorsal fin as a suction pad, it clings to a Mantine’s underside to scavenge for leftovers."),
    ("Octillery", "Jet Pokémon", "Water", "", "It instinctively sneaks into rocky holes. If it gets sleepy, it steals the nest of a fellow Octillery."),
    ("Delibird", "Delivery Pokémon", "Ice", "Flying", "It nests at the edge of sharp cliffs. It spends all day carrying food to its awaiting chicks."),
    ("Mantine", "Kite Pokémon", "Water", "Flying", "Swimming freely in open seas, it may fly out of the water and over the waves if it builds up enough speed."),
    ("Skarmory", "Armor Bird Pokémon", "Steel", "Flying", "After nesting in bramble bushes, the wings of its chicks grow hard from scratches by thorns."),
    ("Houndour", "Dark Pokémon", "Dark", "Fire", "To corner prey, they check each other’s location using barks that only they can understand."),
    ("Houndoom", "Dark Pokémon", "Dark", "Fire", "Upon hearing its eerie howls, other Pokémon get the shivers and head straight back to their nests."),
    ("Kingdra", "Dragon Pokémon", "Water", "Dragon", "It sleeps deep on the ocean floor to build its energy. It is said to cause tornadoes as it wakes."),
    ("Phanpy", "Long Nose Pokémon", "Ground", "", "As a sign of affection, it bumps with its snout. However, it is so strong, it may send you flying."),
    ("Donphan", "Armor Pokémon", "Ground", "", "The longer and bigger its tusks, the higher its rank in its herd. The tusks take a long time to grow."),
    ("Porygon2", "Virtual Pokémon", "Normal", "", "Further research enhanced its abilities. Sometimes, it may exhibit motions that were not programmed."),
    ("Stantler", "Big Horn Pokémon", "Normal", "", "Those who stare at its antlers will gradually lose control of their senses and be unable to stand."),
    ("Smeargle", "Painter Pokémon", "Normal", "", "Once it becomes an adult, it has a tendency to let its comrades plant footprints on its back."),
    ("Tyrogue", "Scuffle Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "Even though it is small, it can’t be ignored because it will slug any handy target without warning."),
    ("Hitmontop", "Handstand Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "It launches kicks while spinning. If it spins at high speed, it may bore its way into the ground."),
    ("Smoochum", "Kiss Pokémon", "Ice", "Psychic", "It always rocks its head slowly backwards and forwards as if it is trying to kiss someone."),
    ("Elekid", "Electric Pokémon", "Electric", "", "Even in the most vicious storm, this Pokémon plays happily if thunder rumbles in the sky."),
    ("Magby", "Live Coal Pokémon", "Fire", "", "It is found in volcanic craters. Its body heat exceeds 1,100 degrees Fahrenheit, so don’t underestimate it."),
    ("Miltank", "Milk Cow Pokémon", "Normal", "", "If it has just had a baby, the milk it produces contains much more nutrition than usual."),
    ("Blissey", "Happiness Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It has a very compassionate nature. If it sees a sick Pokémon, it will nurse the sufferer back to health."),
    ("Raikou", "Thunder Pokémon", "Electric", "", "This Pokémon races across the land while barking a cry that sounds like crashing thunder."),
    ("Entei", "Volcano Pokémon", "Fire", "", "A Pokémon that races across the land. It is said that one is born every time a new volcano appears."),
    ("Suicune", "Aurora Pokémon", "Water", "", "This Pokémon races across the land. It is said that north winds will somehow blow whenever it appears."),
    ("Larvitar", "Rock Skin Pokémon", "Rock", "Ground", "It is born deep underground. It can’t emerge until it has entirely consumed the soil around it."),
    ("Pupitar", "Hard Shell Pokémon", "Rock", "Ground", "Even sealed in its shell, it can move freely. Hard and fast, it has outstanding destructive power."),
    ("Tyranitar", "Armor Pokémon", "Rock", "Dark", "Its body can’t be harmed by any sort of attack, so it is very eager to make challenges against enemies."),
    ("Lugia", "Diving Pokémon", "Psychic", "Flying", "It is said to be the guardian of the seas. It is rumored to have been seen on the night of a storm."),
    ("Ho-Oh", "Rainbow Pokémon", "Fire", "Flying", "A legend says that its body glows in seven colors. A rainbow is said to form behind it when it flies."),
    ("Celebi", "Time Travel Pokémon", "Psychic", "Grass", "When Celebi disappears deep in a forest, it is said to leave behind an egg it brought from the future."),
    ("Treecko", "Wood Gecko Pokémon", "Grass", "", "It quickly scales even vertical walls. It senses humidity with its tail to predict the next day’s weather."),
    ("Grovyle", "Wood Gecko Pokémon", "Grass", "", "Its strongly developed thigh muscles give it astounding agility and jumping performance."),
    ("Sceptile", "Forest Pokémon", "Grass", "", "The leaves on its forelegs are as sharp as swords. It agilely leaps about the branches of trees to strike."),
    ("Torchic", "Chick Pokémon", "Fire", "", "It has a flame sac inside its belly that perpetually burns. It feels warm if it is hugged."),
    ("Combusken", "Young Fowl Pokémon", "Fire", "Fighting", "It boosts its concentration by emitting harsh cries. Its kicks have outstanding destructive power."),
    ("Blaziken", "Blaze Pokémon", "Fire", "Fighting", "When facing a tough foe, it looses flames from its wrists. Its powerful legs let it jump clear over buildings."),
    ("Mudkip", "Mud Fish Pokémon", "Water", "", "Its large tail fin propels it through water with powerful acceleration. It is strong in spite of its size."),
    ("Marshtomp", "Mud Fish Pokémon", "Water", "Ground", "It is at its best when on muddy ground with poor footing. It quickly overwhelms foes struggling in mud."),
    ("Swampert", "Mud Fish Pokémon", "Water", "Ground", "Its arms are rock-hard. With one swing, they can batter down its foe. It makes its nest on beautiful beaches."),
    ("Poochyena", "Bite Pokémon", "Dark", "", "It has a very tenacious nature. Its acute sense of smell lets it chase a chosen prey without ever losing track."),
    ("Mightyena", "Bite Pokémon", "Dark", "", "It will always obey the commands of a skilled Trainer. Its behavior arises from its living in packs in ancient times."),
    ("Zigzagoon", "Tiny Raccoon Pokémon", "Normal", "", "A Pokémon with abundant curiosity. It shows an interest in everything, so it always zigs and zags."),
    ("Linoone", "Rushing Pokémon", "Normal", "", "When running in a straight line, it can top 60 miles per hour. However, it has a tough time with curved roads."),
    ("Wurmple", "Worm Pokémon", "Bug", "", "It lives amidst tall grass and in forests. When attacked, it resists by pointing its venomous spikes at the foe."),
    ("Silcoon", "Cocoon Pokémon", "Bug", "", "It conserves its energy by moving as little as possible. It awaits evolution while drinking only a little rainwater."),
    ("Beautifly", "Butterfly Pokémon", "Bug", "Flying", "Despite its appearance, it has an aggressive nature. It attacks by jabbing with its long, thin mouth."),
    ("Cascoon", "Cocoon Pokémon", "Bug", "", "Its body, which is made of soft silk, hardens over time. When cracks appear, evolution is near."),
    ("Dustox", "Poison Moth Pokémon", "Bug", "Poison", "It scatters horribly toxic dust when it senses danger. They tend to gather in the glow of streetlamps at night."),
    ("Lotad", "Water Weed Pokémon", "Water", "Grass", "It searches about for clean water. If it does not drink water for too long, the leaf on its head wilts."),
    ("Lombre", "Jolly Pokémon", "Water", "Grass", "It lives at the water’s edge where it is sunny. It sleeps on a bed of water grass by day and becomes active at night."),
    ("Ludicolo", "Carefree Pokémon", "Water", "Grass", "The rhythm of bright, festive music activates Ludicolo’s cells, making it more powerful."),
    ("Seedot", "Acorn Pokémon", "Grass", "", "If it remains still, it becomes impossible to distinguish from real nuts. It delights in surprising foraging Pidgey."),
    ("Nuzleaf", "Wily Pokémon", "Grass", "Dark", "They live in holes bored in large trees. The sound of Nuzleaf’s grass flute fills listeners with dread."),
    ("Shiftry", "Wicked Pokémon", "Grass", "Dark", "A Pokémon that was feared as a forest guardian. It can read the foe’s mind and take preemptive action."),
    ("Taillow", "Tiny Swallow Pokémon", "Normal", "Flying", "It dislikes cold seasons. They migrate to other lands in search of warmth, flying over 180 miles a day."),
    ("Swellow", "Swallow Pokémon", "Normal", "Flying", "If its two tail feathers are standing at attention, it is proof of good health. It soars elegantly in the sky."),
    ("Wingull", "Seagull Pokémon", "Water", "Flying", "It rides upon ocean winds as if it were a glider. In the winter, it hides food around its nest."),
    ("Pelipper", "Water Bird Pokémon", "Water", "Flying", "It is a flying transporter that carries small Pokémon in its beak. It bobs on the waves to rest its wings."),
    ("Ralts", "Feeling Pokémon", "Psychic", "Fairy", "It is highly attuned to the emotions of people and Pokémon. It hides if it senses hostility."),
    ("Kirlia", "Emotion Pokémon", "Psychic", "Fairy", "The cheerful spirit of its Trainer gives it energy for its psychokinetic power. It spins and dances when happy."),
    ("Gardevoir", "Embrace Pokémon", "Psychic", "Fairy", "It has the power to predict the future. Its power peaks when it is protecting its Trainer."),
    ("Surskit", "Pond Skater Pokémon", "Bug", "Water", "They usually live on ponds, but after an evening shower, they may appear on puddles in towns."),
    ("Masquerain", "Eyeball Pokémon", "Bug", "Flying", "The antennae have distinctive patterns that look like eyes. When it rains, they grow heavy, making flight impossible."),
    ("Shroomish", "Mushroom Pokémon", "Grass", "", "It prefers damp places. By day it remains still in the forest shade. It releases toxic powder from its head."),
    ("Breloom", "Mushroom Pokémon", "Grass", "Fighting", "The seeds on its tail are made of toxic spores. It knocks out foes with quick, virtually invisible punches."),
    ("Slakoth", "Slacker Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It sleeps for 20 hours every day. Making drowsy those that see it is one of its abilities."),
    ("Vigoroth", "Wild Monkey Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It is always hungry because it won’t stop rampaging. Even while it is eating, it can’t keep still."),
    ("Slaking", "Lazy Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It is the world’s most slothful Pokémon. However, it can exert horrifying power by releasing pent-up energy all at once."),
    ("Nincada", "Trainee Pokémon", "Bug", "Ground", "Because it lived almost entirely underground, it is nearly blind. It uses its antennae instead."),
    ("Ninjask", "Ninja Pokémon", "Bug", "Flying", "This Pokémon is so quick, it is said to be able to avoid any attack. It loves to feed on tree sap."),
    ("Shedinja", "Shed Pokémon", "Bug", "Ghost", "A most peculiar Pokémon that somehow appears in a POKé Ball when a Nincada evolves."),
    ("Whismur", "Whisper Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It usually murmurs, but starts crying loudly if it senses danger. It stops when its ear covers are shut."),
    ("Loudred", "Big Voice Pokémon", "Normal", "", "When it stamps its feet and bellows, it generates ultrasonic waves that can blow apart a house."),
    ("Exploud", "Loud Noise Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It emits a variety of sounds from the holes all over its body. Its loud cries can be heard from over six miles away."),
    ("Makuhita", "Guts Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "It grows stronger by enduring harsh training. It is a gutsy Pokémon that can withstand any attack."),
    ("Hariyama", "Arm Thrust Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "It stomps on the ground to build power. It can send a 10-ton truck flying with a straight-arm punch."),
    ("Azurill", "Polka Dot Pokémon", "Normal", "Fairy", "It battles by flinging around its tail, which is bigger than its body. The tail is a flotation device in water."),
    ("Nosepass", "Compass Pokémon", "Rock", "", "Its magnetic nose consistently faces north. Travelers check Nosepass to get their bearings."),
    ("Skitty", "Kitten Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It is said to be difficult to earn its trust. However, it is extremely popular for its cute looks and behavior."),
    ("Delcatty", "Prim Pokémon", "Normal", "", "The favorite of trend-conscious female Trainers, they are used in competition for their style and fur."),
    ("Sableye", "Darkness Pokémon", "Dark", "Ghost", "It feeds on gemstone crystals. In darkness, its eyes sparkle with the glitter of jewels."),
    ("Mawile", "Deceiver Pokémon", "Steel", "Fairy", "It uses its docile-looking face to lull foes into complacency, then bites with its huge, relentless jaws."),
    ("Aron", "Iron Armor Pokémon", "Steel", "Rock", "It eats iron to build its steel body. It is a pest that descends from mountains to eat bridges and train tracks."),
    ("Lairon", "Iron Armor Pokémon", "Steel", "Rock", "It habitually shows off its strength with the size of sparks it creates by ramming its steel body into boulders."),
    ("Aggron", "Iron Armor Pokémon", "Steel", "Rock", "It claims a large mountain as its sole territory. It mercilessly thrashes those that violate its space."),
    ("Meditite", "Meditate Pokémon", "Fighting", "Psychic", "It never skips its daily yoga training. It heightens its inner strength through meditation."),
    ("Medicham", "Meditate Pokémon", "Fighting", "Psychic", "It elegantly avoids attacks with dance- like steps, then launches a devastating blow in the same motion."),
    ("Electrike", "Lightning Pokémon", "Electric", "", "It stores static electricity in its fur for discharging. It gives off sparks if a storm approaches."),
    ("Manectric", "Discharge Pokémon", "Electric", "", "It rarely appears before people. It is said to nest where lightning has fallen."),
    ("Plusle", "Cheering Pokémon", "Electric", "", "It cheers on partners while scattering sparks from its body. It climbs telephone poles to absorb electricity."),
    ("Minun", "Cheering Pokémon", "Electric", "", "Its dislike of water makes it take shelter under the eaves of houses in rain. It uses pom-poms made of sparks for cheering."),
    ("Volbeat", "Firefly Pokémon", "Bug", "", "It lives around clean ponds. At night, its rear lights up. It converses with others by flashing its light."),
    ("Illumise", "Firefly Pokémon", "Bug", "", "It guides Volbeat to draw signs in night skies. There are scientists that study the patterns it creates."),
    ("Roselia", "Thorn Pokémon", "Grass", "Poison", "Its flowers give off a relaxing fragrance. The stronger its aroma, the healthier the Roselia is."),
    ("Gulpin", "Stomach Pokémon", "Poison", "", "There is nothing its stomach can’t digest. While it is digesting, vile, overpowering gases are expelled."),
    ("Swalot", "Poison Bag Pokémon", "Poison", "", "It can swallow a tire whole in one gulp. It secretes a horribly toxic fluid from the pores on its body."),
    ("Carvanha", "Savage Pokémon", "Water", "Dark", "It lives in massive rivers that course through jungles. It swarms prey that enter its territory."),
    ("Sharpedo", "Brutal Pokémon", "Water", "Dark", "The ruffian of the seas, it has fangs that crunch through iron. It swims by jetting water from its rear."),
    ("Wailmer", "Ball Whale Pokémon", "Water", "", "When it sucks in a large volume of seawater, it becomes like a big, bouncy ball. It eats a ton of food daily."),
    ("Wailord", "Float Whale Pokémon", "Water", "", "It is among the largest of all Pokémon. It herds prey in a pack then swallows the massed prey in one gulp."),
    ("Numel", "Numb Pokémon", "Fire", "Ground", "Magma of almost 2,200 degrees Fahrenheit courses through its body. When it grows cold, the magma hardens and slows it."),
    ("Camerupt", "Eruption Pokémon", "Fire", "Ground", "If angered, the humps on its back erupt in a shower of molten lava. It lives in the craters of volcanoes."),
    ("Torkoal", "Coal Pokémon", "Fire", "", "It burns coal inside its shell. If it is attacked, it belches thick, black smoke and flees."),
    ("Spoink", "Bounce Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "It apparently dies if it stops bouncing about. It carries a pearl from Clamperl on its head."),
    ("Grumpig", "Manipulate Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "It can gain control over foes by doing odd dance steps. The black pearls on its forehead are precious gems."),
    ("Spinda", "Spot Panda Pokémon", "Normal", "", "No two Spinda are said to have identical patterns. It confuses foes with its stumbling motions."),
    ("Trapinch", "Ant Pit Pokémon", "Ground", "", "It lives in arid deserts. It makes a sloping pit trap in sand where it patiently awaits prey."),
    ("Vibrava", "Vibration Pokémon", "Ground", "Dragon", "It generates ultrasonic waves by violently flapping its wings. After making its prey faint, it melts the prey with acid."),
    ("Flygon", "Mystic Pokémon", "Ground", "Dragon", "It hides itself by kicking up desert sand with its wings. Red covers shield its eyes from sand."),
    ("Cacnea", "Cactus Pokémon", "Grass", "", "It prefers harsh environments such as deserts. It can survive for 30 days on water stored in its body."),
    ("Cacturne", "Scarecrow Pokémon", "Grass", "Dark", "It lives in deserts. It becomes active at night when it hunts for prey exhausted from the desert’s heat."),
    ("Swablu", "Cotton Bird Pokémon", "Normal", "Flying", "It constantly grooms its cotton-like wings. It takes a shower to clean itself if it becomes dirty."),
    ("Altaria", "Humming Pokémon", "Dragon", "Flying", "If you hear a beautiful melody trilling deep among mountains far from people, it is Altaria’s humming."),
    ("Zangoose", "Cat Ferret Pokémon", "Normal", "", "If it comes across a Seviper, its fur bristles and it assumes its battle pose. Its sharp claws are its best weapon."),
    ("Seviper", "Fang Snake Pokémon", "Poison", "", "It sharpens its swordlike tail on hard rocks. It hides in tall grass and strikes unwary prey with venomous fangs."),
    ("Lunatone", "Meteorite Pokémon", "Rock", "Psychic", "Its health ebbs and flows with the lunar cycle. It brims with power when exposed to the light of the full moon."),
    ("Solrock", "Meteorite Pokémon", "Rock", "Psychic", "It absorbs solar energy during the day. Always expressionless, it can sense what its foe is thinking."),
    ("Barboach", "Whiskers Pokémon", "Water", "Ground", "It probes muddy riverbeds with its two long whiskers. A slimy film protects its body."),
    ("Whiscash", "Whiskers Pokémon", "Water", "Ground", "It makes its nest at the bottom of swamps. It will eat anything - if it is alive, Whiscash will eat it."),
    ("Corphish", "Ruffian Pokémon", "Water", "", "It came from overseas. It is a very hardy creature that will quickly proliferate, even in polluted streams."),
    ("Crawdaunt", "Rogue Pokémon", "Water", "Dark", "A rough customer that wildly flails its giant claws. It is said to be extremely hard to raise."),
    ("Baltoy", "Clay Doll Pokémon", "Ground", "Psychic", "It was discovered in ancient ruins. While moving, it constantly spins. It stands on one foot even when asleep."),
    ("Claydol", "Clay Doll Pokémon", "Ground", "Psychic", "It appears to have been born from clay dolls made by ancient people. It uses telekinesis to float and move."),
    ("Lileep", "Sea Lily Pokémon", "Rock", "Grass", "It became extinct roughly 100 million years ago. It was regenerated from a fossil using advanced techniques."),
    ("Cradily", "Barnacle Pokémon", "Rock", "Grass", "It ensnares prey with its eight tentacles. It then melts the prey with a strong acid before feeding."),
    ("Anorith", "Old Shrimp Pokémon", "Rock", "Bug", "It is a kind of Pokémon progenitor. It uses its extending claws to catch prey hiding among rocks on the seafloor."),
    ("Armaldo", "Plate Pokémon", "Rock", "Bug", "Protected by a hard shell, its body is very sturdy. It skewers prey with its claws to feed."),
    ("Feebas", "Fish Pokémon", "Water", "", "Ridiculed for its shabby appearance, it is ignored by researchers. It lives in ponds choked with weeds."),
    ("Milotic", "Tender Pokémon", "Water", "", "Milotic is breathtakingly beautiful. Those that see it are said to forget their combative spirits."),
    ("Castform", "Weather Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It has the ability to change its form into the sun, the rain, or a snow cloud, depending on the weather."),
    ("Kecleon", "Color Swap Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It changes body color to blend in with its surroundings. It also changes color if it is happy or sad."),
    ("Shuppet", "Puppet Pokémon", "Ghost", "", "It loves to feed on feelings like envy and malice. Its upright horn catches the emotions of people."),
    ("Banette", "Marionette Pokémon", "Ghost", "", "Strong feelings of hatred turned a puppet into a Pokémon. If it opens its mouth, its cursed energy escapes."),
    ("Duskull", "Requiem Pokémon", "Ghost", "", "Making itself invisible, it silently sneaks up to prey. It has the ability to slip through thick walls."),
    ("Dusclops", "Beckon Pokémon", "Ghost", "", "Its body is entirely hollow. When it opens its mouth, it sucks everything in as if it were a black hole."),
    ("Tropius", "Fruit Pokémon", "Grass", "Flying", "It lives in tropical jungles. The bunch of fruit around its neck is delicious. The fruit grows twice a year."),
    ("Chimecho", "Wind Chime Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "It travels by riding on winds. It cleverly uses its long tail to pluck nuts and berries, which it loves to eat."),
    ("Absol", "Disaster Pokémon", "Dark", "", "It appears when it senses an impending natural disaster. As a result, it was mistaken as a doom-bringer."),
    ("Wynaut", "Bright Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "It tends to move in a pack with others. They cluster in a tight group to sleep in a cave."),
    ("Snorunt", "Snow Hat Pokémon", "Ice", "", "It is said that a home visited by a Snorunt will prosper. It can withstand cold of minus 150 degrees Fahrenheit."),
    ("Glalie", "Face Pokémon", "Ice", "", "It has a body of ice that won’t melt, even with fire. It can instantly freeze moisture in the atmosphere."),
    ("Spheal", "Clap Pokémon", "Ice", "Water", "Its body is covered in fluffy fur. The fur keeps it from feeling cold while it is rolling on ice."),
    ("Sealeo", "Ball Roll Pokémon", "Ice", "Water", "It touches new things with its nose to test for smell and feel. It plays by spinning Spheal on its nose."),
    ("Walrein", "Ice Break Pokémon", "Ice", "Water", "It swims through icy seas while shattering ice floes with its large tusks. It is protected by its thick blubber."),
    ("Clamperl", "Bivalve Pokémon", "Water", "", "It is protected by a sturdy shell. Once in a lifetime, it makes a magnificent pearl."),
    ("Huntail", "Deep Sea Pokémon", "Water", "", "It lives deep in the sea where no light ever filters down. It lights up its small fishlike tail to attract prey."),
    ("Gorebyss", "South Sea Pokémon", "Water", "", "Its swimming form is exquisitely elegant. With its thin mouth, it feeds on seaweed that grows between rocks."),
    ("Relicanth", "Longevity Pokémon", "Water", "Rock", "It has remained unchanged for 100 million years. It was discovered during a deep-sea exploration."),
    ("Luvdisc", "Rendezvous Pokémon", "Water", "", "During the spawning season, countless Luvdisc congregate at coral reefs, turning the waters pink."),
    ("Bagon", "Rock Head Pokémon", "Dragon", "", "Its steel-hard head can shatter boulders. It longingly hopes for wings to grow so it can fly."),
    ("Shelgon", "Endurance Pokémon", "Dragon", "", "Its armored body makes all attacks bounce off. The armor is too tough, however, making it heavy and somewhat sluggish."),
    ("Salamence", "Dragon Pokémon", "Dragon", "Flying", "It becomes uncontrollable if it is enraged. It destroys everything with shredding claws and fire."),
    ("Beldum", "Iron Ball Pokémon", "Steel", "Psychic", "It uses magnetic waves to converse with its kind. All the cells in its body are magnetic."),
    ("Metang", "Iron Claw Pokémon", "Steel", "Psychic", "It floats midair using magnetism. Its body is so tough, even a crash with a jet plane won’t leave a scratch."),
    ("Metagross", "Iron Leg Pokémon", "Steel", "Psychic", "It is formed by two Metang fusing. Its four brains are said to be superior to a supercomputer."),
    ("Regirock", "Rock Peak Pokémon", "Rock", "", "It is entirely composed of rocks with no sign of a brain or heart. It is a mystery even to modern scientists."),
    ("Regice", "Iceberg Pokémon", "Ice", "", "Research revealed that its body is made of the same kind of ice that is found at the South Pole."),
    ("Registeel", "Iron Pokémon", "Steel", "", "It is sturdier than any kind of metal. It hardened due to pressure underground over tens of thousands of years."),
    ("Latias", "Eon Pokémon", "Dragon", "Psychic", "It can telepathically communicate with people. It changes its appearance using its down that refracts light."),
    ("Latios", "Eon Pokémon", "Dragon", "Psychic", "It has a docile temperament and dislikes fighting. Tucking in its forelegs, it can fly faster than a jet plane."),
    ("Kyogre", "Sea Basin Pokémon", "Water", "", "This Pokémon is said to have expanded the sea by bringing heavy rains. It has the power to control water."),
    ("Groudon", "Continent Pokémon", "Ground", "", "This legendary Pokémon is said to represent the land. It went to sleep after dueling Kyogre."),
    ("Rayquaza", "Sky High Pokémon", "Dragon", "Flying", "It has lived for hundreds of millions of years in the ozone layer. Its flying form looks like a meteor."),
    ("Jirachi", "Wish Pokémon", "Steel", "Psychic", "It is said to make any wish come true. It is awake for only seven days out of a thousand years."),
    ("Deoxys", "DNA Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "This Deoxys has transformed into its aggressive guise. It can fool enemies by altering its appearance."),
    ("Turtwig", "Tiny Leaf Pokémon", "Grass", "", "Made from soil, the shell on its back hardens when it drinks water. It lives along lakes."),
    ("Grotle", "Grove Pokémon", "Grass", "", "It lives along water in forests. In the daytime, it leaves the forest to sunbathe its treed shell."),
    ("Torterra", "Continent Pokémon", "Grass", "Ground", "Small Pokémon occasionally gather on its unmoving back to begin building their nests."),
    ("Chimchar", "Chimp Pokémon", "Fire", "", "It agilely scales sheer cliffs to live atop craggy mountains. Its fire is put out when it sleeps."),
    ("Monferno", "Playful Pokémon", "Fire", "Fighting", "To intimidate attackers, it stretches the fire on its tail to make itself appear bigger."),
    ("Infernape", "Flame Pokémon", "Fire", "Fighting", "It uses a special kind of martial arts involving all its limbs. Its fire never goes out."),
    ("Piplup", "Penguin Pokémon", "Water", "", "Because it is very proud, it hates accepting food from people. Its thick down guards it from cold."),
    ("Prinplup", "Penguin Pokémon", "Water", "", "It lives alone, away from others. Apparently, every one of them believes it is the most important."),
    ("Empoleon", "Emperor Pokémon", "Water", "Steel", "The three horns that extend from its beak attest to its power. The leader has the biggest horns."),
    ("Starly", "Starling Pokémon", "Normal", "Flying", "They flock in great numbers. Though small, they flap their wings with great power."),
    ("Staravia", "Starling Pokémon", "Normal", "Flying", "It flies around forests and fields in search of bug Pokémon. It stays within a huge flock."),
    ("Staraptor", "Predator Pokémon", "Normal", "Flying", "It has a savage nature. It will courageously challenge foes that are much larger."),
    ("Bidoof", "Plump Mouse Pokémon", "Normal", "", "With nerves of steel, nothing can perturb it. It is more agile and active than it appears."),
    ("Bibarel", "Beaver Pokémon", "Normal", "Water", "It makes its nest by damming streams with bark and mud. It is known as an industrious worker."),
    ("Kricketot", "Cricket Pokémon", "Bug", "", "It shakes its head back to front, causing its antennae to hit each other and sound like a xylophone."),
    ("Kricketune", "Cricket Pokémon", "Bug", "", "It crosses its knifelike arms in front of its chest when it cries. It can compose melodies ad lib."),
    ("Shinx", "Flash Pokémon", "Electric", "", "All of its fur dazzles if danger is sensed. It flees while the foe is momentarily blinded."),
    ("Luxio", "Spark Pokémon", "Electric", "", "Its claws loose electricity with enough amperage to cause fainting. They live in small groups."),
    ("Luxray", "Gleam Eyes Pokémon", "Electric", "", "It has eyes that can see through anything. It spots and captures prey hiding behind objects."),
    ("Budew", "Bud Pokémon", "Grass", "Poison", "Over the winter, it closes its bud and endures the cold. In spring, the bud opens and releases pollen."),
    ("Roserade", "Bouquet Pokémon", "Grass", "Poison", "It attracts prey with a sweet aroma, then downs it with thorny whips hidden in its arms."),
    ("Cranidos", "Head Butt Pokémon", "Rock", "", "It lived in jungles around 100 million years ago. Its skull is as hard as iron."),
    ("Rampardos", "Head Butt Pokémon", "Rock", "", "Its powerful head butt has enough power to shatter even the most durable things upon impact."),
    ("Shieldon", "Shield Pokémon", "Rock", "Steel", "A Pokémon that lived in jungles around 100 million years ago. Its facial hide is extremely hard."),
    ("Bastiodon", "Shield Pokémon", "Rock", "Steel", "Any frontal attack is repulsed. It is a docile Pokémon that feeds on grass and berries."),
    ("Burmy", "Bagworm Pokémon", "Bug", "", "To shelter itself from cold, wintry winds, it covers itself with a cloak made of twigs and leaves."),
    ("Wormadam", "Bagworm Pokémon", "Bug", "Grass", "When Burmy evolved, its cloak became a part of this Pokémon’s body. The cloak is never shed."),
    ("Mothim", "Moth Pokémon", "Bug", "Flying", "It loves the honey of flowers and steals honey collected by Combee."),
    ("Combee", "Tiny Bee Pokémon", "Bug", "Flying", "A Pokémon formed by three others. It busily carries sweet floral honey to Vespiquen."),
    ("Vespiquen", "Beehive Pokémon", "Bug", "Flying", "Its abdomen is a honeycomb for grubs. It raises its grubs on honey collected by Combee."),
    ("Pachirisu", "EleSquirrel Pokémon", "Electric", "", "It makes fur balls that crackle with static electricity. It stores them with berries in tree holes."),
    ("Buizel", "Sea Weasel Pokémon", "Water", "", "It has a flotation sac that is like an inflatable collar. It floats on water with its head out."),
    ("Floatzel", "Sea Weasel Pokémon", "Water", "", "It floats using its well-developed flotation sac. It assists in the rescues of drowning people."),
    ("Cherubi", "Cherry Pokémon", "Grass", "", "The small ball holds the nutrients needed for evolution. Apparently, it is very sweet and tasty."),
    ("Cherrim", "Blossom Pokémon", "Grass", "", "It blooms during times of strong sunlight. It tries to make up for everything it endured as a bud."),
    ("Shellos", "Sea Slug Pokémon", "Water", "", "Its colors and shapes differ from region to region. In the Sinnoh region, two types are confirmed."),
    ("Gastrodon", "Sea Slug Pokémon", "Water", "Ground", "It has a pliable body without any bones. If any part of its body is torn off, it grows right back."),
    ("Ambipom", "Long Tail Pokémon", "Normal", "", "To eat, it deftly shucks nuts with its two tails. It rarely uses its arms now."),
    ("Drifloon", "Balloon Pokémon", "Ghost", "Flying", "A Pokémon formed by the spirits of people and Pokémon. It loves damp, humid seasons."),
    ("Drifblim", "Blimp Pokémon", "Ghost", "Flying", "It’s drowzy in daytime, but flies off in the evening in big groups. No one knows where they go."),
    ("Buneary", "Rabbit Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It slams foes by sharply uncoiling its rolled ears. It stings enough to make a grown-up cry in pain."),
    ("Lopunny", "Rabbit Pokémon", "Normal", "", "An extremely cautious Pokémon. It cloaks its body with its fluffy ear fur when it senses danger."),
    ("Mismagius", "Magical Pokémon", "Ghost", "", "Its cries sound like incantations. Those hearing it are tormented by headaches and hallucinations."),
    ("Honchkrow", "Big Boss Pokémon", "Dark", "Flying", "Becoming active at night, it is known to swarm with numerous Murkrow in tow."),
    ("Glameow", "Catty Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It claws if displeased and purrs when affectionate. Its fickleness is very popular among some."),
    ("Purugly", "Tiger Cat Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It is a brazen brute that barges its way into another Pokémon’s nest and claims it as its own."),
    ("Chingling", "Bell Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "It emits cries by agitating an orb at the back of its throat. It moves with flouncing hops."),
    ("Stunky", "Skunk Pokémon", "Poison", "Dark", "It protects itself by spraying a noxious fluid from its rear. The stench lingers for 24 hours."),
    ("Skuntank", "Skunk Pokémon", "Poison", "Dark", "It sprays a vile-smelling fluid from the tip of its tail to attack. Its range is over 160 feet."),
    ("Bronzor", "Bronze Pokémon", "Steel", "Psychic", "Implements shaped like it were discovered in ancient tombs. It is unknown if they are related."),
    ("Bronzong", "Bronze Bell Pokémon", "Steel", "Psychic", "One caused a news sensation when it was dug up at a construction site after a 2,000-year sleep."),
    ("Bonsly", "Bonsai Pokémon", "Rock", "", "It looks as if it is always crying. It is actually adjusting its body’s fluid levels by eliminating excess."),
    ("Mime Jr.", "Mime Pokémon", "Psychic", "Fairy", "It habitually mimics foes. Once mimicked, the foe cannot take its eyes off this Pokémon."),
    ("Happiny", "Playhouse Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It loves round white things. It carries an egg-shaped rock in imitation of Chansey."),
    ("Chatot", "Music Note Pokémon", "Normal", "Flying", "It can learn and speak human words. If they gather, they all learn the same saying."),
    ("Spiritomb", "Forbidden Pokémon", "Ghost", "Dark", "A Pokémon that was formed by 108 spirits. It is bound to a fissure in an odd keystone."),
    ("Gible", "Land Shark Pokémon", "Dragon", "Ground", "It nests in small, horizontal holes in cave walls. It pounces to catch prey that stray too close."),
    ("Gabite", "Cave Pokémon", "Dragon", "Ground", "There is a long-held belief that medicine made from its scales will heal even incurable illnesses."),
    ("Garchomp", "Mach Pokémon", "Dragon", "Ground", "When it folds up its body and extends its wings, it looks like a jet plane. It flies at sonic speed."),
    ("Munchlax", "Big Eater Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It wolfs down its weight in food once a day, swallowing food whole with almost no chewing."),
    ("Riolu", "Emanation Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "The aura that emanates from its body intensifies to alert others if it is afraid or sad."),
    ("Lucario", "Aura Pokémon", "Fighting", "Steel", "It has the ability to sense the auras of all things. It understands human speech."),
    ("Hippopotas", "Hippo Pokémon", "Ground", "", "It lives in arid places. Instead of perspiration, it expels grainy sand from its body."),
    ("Hippowdon", "Heavyweight Pokémon", "Ground", "", "It blasts internally stored sand from ports on its body to create a towering twister for attack."),
    ("Skorupi", "Scorpion Pokémon", "Poison", "Bug", "It grips prey with its tail claws and injects poison. It tenaciously hangs on until the poison takes."),
    ("Drapion", "Ogre Scorpion Pokémon", "Poison", "Dark", "It has the power in its clawed arms to make scrap of a car. The tips of its claws release poison."),
    ("Croagunk", "Toxic Mouth Pokémon", "Poison", "Fighting", "Its cheeks hold poison sacs. It tries to catch foes off guard to jab them with toxic fingers."),
    ("Toxicroak", "Toxic Mouth Pokémon", "Poison", "Fighting", "Its knuckle claws secrete a toxin so vile that even a scratch could prove fatal."),
    ("Carnivine", "Bug Catcher Pokémon", "Grass", "", "It attracts prey with its sweet- smelling saliva, then chomps down. It takes a whole day to eat prey."),
    ("Finneon", "Wing Fish Pokémon", "Water", "", "After long exposure to sunlight, the patterns on its tail fins shine vividly when darkness arrives."),
    ("Lumineon", "Neon Pokémon", "Water", "", "It lives on the deep-sea floor. It attracts prey by flashing the patterns on its four tail fins."),
    ("Mantyke", "Kite Pokémon", "Water", "Flying", "A friendly Pokémon that captures the subtle flows of seawater using its two antennae."),
    ("Snover", "Frost Tree Pokémon", "Grass", "Ice", "It lives on snowy mountains. Having had little contact with humans, it is boldly inquisitive."),
    ("Abomasnow", "Frost Tree Pokémon", "Grass", "Ice", "It whips up blizzards in mountains that are always buried in snow. It is the abominable snowman."),
    ("Weavile", "Sharp Claw Pokémon", "Dark", "Ice", "They live in cold regions, forming groups of four or five that hunt prey with impressive coordination."),
    ("Magnezone", "Magnet Area Pokémon", "Electric", "Steel", "It evolved from exposure to a special magnetic field. Three units generate magnetism."),
    ("Lickilicky", "Licking Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It wraps things with its extensible tongue. Getting too close to it will leave you soaked with drool."),
    ("Rhyperior", "Drill Pokémon", "Ground", "Rock", "It puts rocks in holes in its palms and uses its muscles to shoot them. Geodude are shot at rare times."),
    ("Tangrowth", "Vine Pokémon", "Grass", "", "It ensnares prey by extending arms made of vines. Losing arms to predators does not trouble it."),
    ("Electivire", "Thunderbolt Pokémon", "Electric", "", "It pushes the tips of its two tails against the foe, then lets loose with over 20,000 volts of power."),
    ("Magmortar", "Blast Pokémon", "Fire", "", "It blasts fireballs of over 3,600 degrees F from the ends of its arms. It lives in volcanic craters."),
    ("Togekiss", "Jubilee Pokémon", "Fairy", "Flying", "It will never appear where there is strife. Its sightings have become rare recently."),
    ("Yanmega", "Ogre Darner Pokémon", "Bug", "Flying", "By churning its wings, it creates shock waves that inflict critical internal injuries to foes."),
    ("Leafeon", "Verdant Pokémon", "Grass", "", "Just like a plant, it uses photosynthesis. As a result, it is always enveloped in clear air."),
    ("Glaceon", "Fresh Snow Pokémon", "Ice", "", "As a protective technique, it can completely freeze its fur to make its hairs stand like needles."),
    ("Gliscor", "Fang Scorpion Pokémon", "Ground", "Flying", "It observes prey while hanging inverted from branches. When the chance presents itself, it swoops!"),
    ("Mamoswine", "Twin Tusk Pokémon", "Ice", "Ground", "Its impressive tusks are made of ice. The population thinned when it turned warm after the ice age."),
    ("Porygon-Z", "Virtual Pokémon", "Normal", "", "Additional software was installed to make it a better Pokémon. It began acting oddly, however."),
    ("Gallade", "Blade Pokémon", "Psychic", "Fighting", "A master of courtesy and swordsmanship, it fights using extending swords on its elbows."),
    ("Probopass", "Compass Pokémon", "Rock", "Steel", "It exudes strong magnetism from all over. It controls three small units called Mini-Noses."),
    ("Dusknoir", "Gripper Pokémon", "Ghost", "", "The antenna on its head captures radio waves from the world of spirits that command it to take people there."),
    ("Froslass", "Snow Land Pokémon", "Ice", "Ghost", "It freezes foes with an icy breath nearly -60 degrees F. What seems to be its body is actually hollow."),
    ("Rotom", "Plasma Pokémon", "Electric", "Ghost", "Its body is composed of plasma. It is known to infiltrate electronic devices and wreak havoc."),
    ("Uxie", "Knowledge Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "Known as “The Being of Knowledge.” It is said that it can wipe out the memory of those who see its eyes."),
    ("Mesprit", "Emotion Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "Known as “The Being of Emotion.” It taught humans the nobility of sorrow, pain, and joy."),
    ("Azelf", "Willpower Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "Known as “The Being of Willpower.” It sleeps at the bottom of a lake to keep the world in balance."),
    ("Dialga", "Temporal Pokémon", "Steel", "Dragon", "It has the power to control time. It appears in Sinnoh-region myths as an ancient deity."),
    ("Palkia", "Spatial Pokémon", "Water", "Dragon", "It has the ability to distort space. It is described as a deity in Sinnoh-region mythology."),
    ("Heatran", "Lava Dome Pokémon", "Fire", "Steel", "It dwells in volcanic caves. It digs in with its cross-shaped feet to crawl on ceilings and walls."),
    ("Regigigas", "Colossal Pokémon", "Normal", "", "There is an enduring legend that states this Pokémon towed continents with ropes."),
    ("Giratina", "Renegade Pokémon", "Ghost", "Dragon", "A Pokémon that is said to live in a world on the reverse side of ours. It appears in an ancient cemetery."),
    ("Cresselia", "Lunar Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "Shiny particles are released from its wings like a veil. It is said to represent the crescent moon."),
    ("Phione", "Sea Drifter Pokémon", "Water", "", "A Pokémon that lives in warm seas. It inflates the flotation sac on its head to drift and search for food."),
    ("Manaphy", "Seafaring Pokémon", "Water", "", "Born on a cold seafloor, it will swim great distances to return to its birthplace."),
    ("Darkrai", "Pitch-Black Pokémon", "Dark", "", "It can lull people to sleep and make them dream. It is active during nights of the new moon."),
    ("Shaymin", "Gratitude Pokémon", "Grass", "", "It lives in flower patches and avoids detection by curling up to look like a flowering plant."),
    ("Arceus", "Alpha Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It is described in mythology as the Pokémon that shaped the universe with its 1,000 arms."),
    ("Victini", "Victory Pokémon", "Psychic", "Fire", "This Pokémon brings victory. It is said that Trainers with Victini always win, regardless of the type of encounter."),
    ("Snivy", "Grass Snake Pokémon", "Grass", "", "It is very intelligent and calm. Being exposed to lots of sunlight makes its movements swifter."),
    ("Servine", "Grass Snake Pokémon", "Grass", "", "It moves along the ground as if sliding. Its swift movements befuddle its foes, and it then attacks with a vine whip."),
    ("Serperior", "Regal Pokémon", "Grass", "", "It can stop its opponents’ movements with just a glare. It takes in solar energy and boosts it internally."),
    ("Tepig", "Fire Pig Pokémon", "Fire", "", "It can deftly dodge its foe’s attacks while shooting fireballs from its nose. It roasts berries before it eats them."),
    ("Pignite", "Fire Pig Pokémon", "Fire", "Fighting", "When its internal fire flares up, its movements grow sharper and faster. When in trouble, it emits smoke."),
    ("Emboar", "Mega Fire Pig Pokémon", "Fire", "Fighting", "It can throw a fire punch by setting its fists on fire with its fiery chin. It cares deeply about its friends."),
    ("Oshawott", "Sea Otter Pokémon", "Water", "", "It fights using the scalchop on its stomach. In response to an attack, it retaliates immediately by slashing."),
    ("Dewott", "Discipline Pokémon", "Water", "", "Strict training is how it learns its flowing double-scalchop technique."),
    ("Samurott", "Formidable Pokémon", "Water", "", "One swing of the sword incorporated in its armor can fell an opponent. A simple glare from one of them quiets everybody."),
    ("Patrat", "Scout Pokémon", "Normal", "", "Using food stored in cheek pouches, they can keep watch for days. They use their tails to communicate with others."),
    ("Watchog", "Lookout Pokémon", "Normal", "", "When they see an enemy, their tails stand high, and they spit the seeds of berries stored in their cheek pouches."),
    ("Lillipup", "Puppy Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It faces strong opponents with great courage. But, when at a disadvantage in a fight, this intelligent Pokémon flees."),
    ("Herdier", "Loyal Dog Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It has black, cape-like fur that is very hard and decreases the amount of damage it receives."),
    ("Stoutland", "Big-Hearted Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It rescues people stranded by blizzards in the mountains. Its shaggy fur shields it from the cold."),
    ("Purrloin", "Devious Pokémon", "Dark", "", "They steal from people for fun, but their victims can’t help but forgive them. Their deceptively cute act is perfect."),
    ("Liepard", "Cruel Pokémon", "Dark", "", "These Pokémon vanish and appear unexpectedly. Many Trainers are drawn to their beautiful form and fur."),
    ("Pansage", "Grass Monkey Pokémon", "Grass", "", "This Pokémon dwells deep in the forest. Eating a leaf from its head whisks weariness away as if by magic."),
    ("Simisage", "Thorn Monkey Pokémon", "Grass", "", "Ill tempered, it fights by swinging its barbed tail around wildly. The leaf growing on its head is very bitter."),
    ("Pansear", "High Temp Pokémon", "Fire", "", "When it is angered, the temperature of its head tuft reaches 600° F. It uses its tuft to roast berries."),
    ("Simisear", "Ember Pokémon", "Fire", "", "It loves sweets because they become energy for the fire burning inside its body."),
    ("Panpour", "Spray Pokémon", "Water", "", "The water stored inside the tuft on its head is full of nutrients. Plants that receive its water grow large."),
    ("Simipour", "Geyser Pokémon", "Water", "", "The tuft on its head holds water. When the level runs low, it replenishes the tuft by siphoning up water with its tail."),
    ("Munna", "Dream Eater Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "Munna always float in the air. People whose dreams are eaten by them forget what the dreams had been about."),
    ("Musharna", "Drowsing Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "The mist emanating from their foreheads is packed with the dreams of people and Pokémon."),
    ("Pidove", "Tiny Pigeon Pokémon", "Normal", "Flying", "Each follows its Trainer’s orders as best it can, but they sometimes fail to understand complicated commands."),
    ("Tranquill", "Wild Pigeon Pokémon", "Normal", "Flying", "It can return to its Trainer’s location regardless of the distance separating them."),
    ("Unfezant", "Proud Pokémon", "Normal", "Flying", "Males swing their head plumage to threaten opponents. The females’ flying abilities surpass those of the males."),
    ("Blitzle", "Electrified Pokémon", "Electric", "", "Its mane shines when it discharges electricity. They use their flashing manes to communicate with one another."),
    ("Zebstrika", "Thunderbolt Pokémon", "Electric", "", "They have lightning-like movements. When Zebstrika run at full speed, the sound of thunder reverberates."),
    ("Roggenrola", "Mantle Pokémon", "Rock", "", "Its ear is hexagonal in shape. Compressed underground, its body is as hard as steel."),
    ("Boldore", "Ore Pokémon", "Rock", "", "When it overflows with power, the orange crystal on its body glows. It looks for underground water in caves."),
    ("Gigalith", "Compressed Pokémon", "Rock", "", "Compressing the energy from its internal core lets it fire off an attack capable of blowing away a mountain."),
    ("Woobat", "Bat Pokémon", "Psychic", "Flying", "Its habitat is dark forests and caves. It emits ultrasonic waves from its nose to learn about its surroundings."),
    ("Swoobat", "Courting Pokémon", "Psychic", "Flying", "It emits sound waves of various frequencies from its nose, including some powerful enough to destroy rocks."),
    ("Drilbur", "Mole Pokémon", "Ground", "", "It can dig through the ground at a speed of 30 mph. It could give a car running aboveground a good race."),
    ("Excadrill", "Subterrene Pokémon", "Ground", "Steel", "It can help in tunnel construction. Its drill has evolved into steel strong enough to bore through iron plates."),
    ("Audino", "Hearing Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It touches others with the feelers on its ears, using the sound of their heartbeats to tell how they are feeling."),
    ("Timburr", "Muscular Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "It fights by swinging a piece of lumber around. It is close to evolving when it can handle the lumber without difficulty."),
    ("Gurdurr", "Muscular Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "This Pokémon is so muscular and strongly built that even a group of wrestlers could not make it budge an inch."),
    ("Conkeldurr", "Muscular Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "It is thought that Conkeldurr taught humans how to make concrete more than 2,000 years ago."),
    ("Tympole", "Tadpole Pokémon", "Water", "", "They warn others of danger by vibrating their cheeks to create a high-pitched sound."),
    ("Palpitoad", "Vibration Pokémon", "Water", "Ground", "When they vibrate the bumps on their heads, they can make waves in water or earthquake-like vibrations on land."),
    ("Seismitoad", "Vibration Pokémon", "Water", "Ground", "They shoot paralyzing liquid from their head bumps. They use vibration to hurt their opponents."),
    ("Throh", "Judo Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "When it tightens its belt, it becomes stronger. Wild Throh use vines to weave their own belts."),
    ("Sawk", "Karate Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "The sound of Sawk punching boulders and trees can be heard all the way from the mountains where they train."),
    ("Sewaddle", "Sewing Pokémon", "Bug", "Grass", "Leavanny dress it in clothes they made for it when it hatched. It hides its head in its hood while it is sleeping."),
    ("Swadloon", "Leaf-Wrapped Pokémon", "Bug", "Grass", "Forests where Swadloon live have superb foliage because the nutrients they make from fallen leaves nourish the plant life."),
    ("Leavanny", "Nurturing Pokémon", "Bug", "Grass", "Upon finding a small Pokémon, it weaves clothing for it from leaves, using the cutters on its arms and sticky silk."),
    ("Venipede", "Centipede Pokémon", "Bug", "Poison", "Its bite injects a potent poison, enough to paralyze large bird Pokémon that try to prey on it."),
    ("Whirlipede", "Curlipede Pokémon", "Bug", "Poison", "Protected by a hard shell, it spins its body like a wheel and crashes furiously into its enemies."),
    ("Scolipede", "Megapede Pokémon", "Bug", "Poison", "With quick movements, it chases down its foes, attacking relentlessly with its horns until it prevails."),
    ("Cottonee", "Cotton Puff Pokémon", "Grass", "Fairy", "When attacked, it escapes by shooting cotton from its body. The cotton serves as a decoy to distract the attacker."),
    ("Whimsicott", "Windveiled Pokémon", "Grass", "Fairy", "Like the wind, it can slip through any gap, no matter how small. It leaves balls of white fluff behind."),
    ("Petilil", "Bulb Pokémon", "Grass", "", "The leaves on its head are very bitter. Eating one of these leaves is known to refresh a tired body."),
    ("Lilligant", "Flowering Pokémon", "Grass", "", "Even veteran Trainers face a challenge in getting its beautiful flower to bloom. This Pokémon is popular with celebrities."),
    ("Basculin", "Hostile Pokémon", "Water", "", "Red and blue Basculin get along so poorly, they’ll start fighting instantly. These Pokémon are very hostile."),
    ("Sandile", "Desert Croc Pokémon", "Ground", "Dark", "They live buried in the sands of the desert. The sun-warmed sands prevent their body temperature from dropping."),
    ("Krokorok", "Desert Croc Pokémon", "Ground", "Dark", "They live in groups of a few individuals. Protective membranes shield their eyes from sandstorms."),
    ("Krookodile", "Intimidation Pokémon", "Ground", "Dark", "They never allow prey to escape. Their jaws are so powerful, they can crush the body of an automobile."),
    ("Darumaka", "Zen Charm Pokémon", "Fire", "", "When its internal fire is burning, it cannot calm down and it runs around. When the fire diminishes, it falls asleep."),
    ("Darmanitan", "Blazing Pokémon", "Fire", "", "Its internal fire burns at 2,500° F, making enough power that it can destroy a dump truck with one punch."),
    ("Maractus", "Cactus Pokémon", "Grass", "", "It uses an up-tempo song and dance to drive away the bird Pokémon that prey on its flower seeds."),
    ("Dwebble", "Rock Inn Pokémon", "Bug", "Rock", "This Pokémon can easily melt holes in hard rocks with a liquid secreted from its mouth."),
    ("Crustle", "Stone Home Pokémon", "Bug", "Rock", "Competing for territory, Crustle fight viciously. The one whose boulder is broken is the loser of the battle."),
    ("Scraggy", "Shedding Pokémon", "Dark", "Fighting", "Its skin has a rubbery elasticity, so it can reduce damage by defensively pulling its skin up to its neck."),
    ("Scrafty", "Hoodlum Pokémon", "Dark", "Fighting", "Groups of them beat up anything that enters their territory. Each can spit acidic liquid from its mouth."),
    ("Sigilyph", "Avianoid Pokémon", "Psychic", "Flying", "They never vary the route they fly, because their memories of guarding an ancient city remain steadfast."),
    ("Yamask", "Spirit Pokémon", "Ghost", "", "Each of them carries a mask that used to be its face when it was human. Sometimes they look at it and cry."),
    ("Cofagrigus", "Coffin Pokémon", "Ghost", "", "It has been said that they swallow those who get too close and turn them into mummies. They like to eat gold nuggets."),
    ("Tirtouga", "Prototurtle Pokémon", "Water", "Rock", "Restored from a fossil, this Pokémon can dive to depths beyond half a mile."),
    ("Carracosta", "Prototurtle Pokémon", "Water", "Rock", "They can live both in the ocean and on land. A slap from one of them is enough to open a hole in the bottom of a tanker."),
    ("Archen", "First Bird Pokémon", "Rock", "Flying", "Said to be an ancestor of bird Pokémon, they were unable to fly and moved about by hopping from one branch to another."),
    ("Archeops", "First Bird Pokémon", "Rock", "Flying", "They are intelligent and will cooperate to catch prey. From the ground, they use a running start to take flight."),
    ("Trubbish", "Trash Bag Pokémon", "Poison", "", "Inhaling the gas they belch will make you sleep for a week. They prefer unsanitary places."),
    ("Garbodor", "Trash Heap Pokémon", "Poison", "", "It clenches opponents with its left arm and finishes them off with foul-smelling poison gas belched from its mouth."),
    ("Zorua", "Tricky Fox Pokémon", "Dark", "", "It changes into the forms of others to surprise them. Apparently, it often transforms into a silent child."),
    ("Zoroark", "Illusion Fox Pokémon", "Dark", "", "Bonds between these Pokémon are very strong. It protects the safety of its pack by tricking its opponents."),
    ("Minccino", "Chinchilla Pokémon", "Normal", "", "They greet one another by rubbing each other with their tails, which are always kept well groomed and clean."),
    ("Cinccino", "Scarf Pokémon", "Normal", "", "Their white fur is coated in a special oil that makes it easy for them to deflect attacks."),
    ("Gothita", "Fixation Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "Their ribbonlike feelers increase their psychic power. They are always staring at something."),
    ("Gothorita", "Manipulate Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "They use hypnosis to control people and Pokémon. Tales of Gothorita leading people astray are told in every corner."),
    ("Gothitelle", "Astral Body Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "Starry skies thousands of light-years away are visible in the space distorted by their intense psychic power."),
    ("Solosis", "Cell Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "They drive away attackers by unleashing psychic power. They can use telepathy to talk with others."),
    ("Duosion", "Mitosis Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "Since they have two divided brains, at times they suddenly try to take two different actions at once."),
    ("Reuniclus", "Multiplying Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "When Reuniclus shake hands, a network forms between their brains, increasing their psychic power."),
    ("Ducklett", "Water Bird Pokémon", "Water", "Flying", "These bird Pokémon are excellent divers. They swim around in the water eating their favorite food--peat moss."),
    ("Swanna", "White Bird Pokémon", "Water", "Flying", "Swanna start to dance at dusk. The one dancing in the middle is the leader of the flock."),
    ("Vanillite", "Fresh Snow Pokémon", "Ice", "", "The temperature of their breath is -58° F. They create snow crystals and make snow fall in the areas around them."),
    ("Vanillish", "Icy Snow Pokémon", "Ice", "", "Snowy mountains are this Pokémon’s habitat. During an ancient ice age, they moved to southern areas."),
    ("Vanilluxe", "Snowstorm Pokémon", "Ice", "", "Swallowing large amounts of water, they make snow clouds inside their bodies and attack their foes with violent blizzards."),
    ("Deerling", "Season Pokémon", "Normal", "Grass", "The color and scent of their fur changes to match the mountain grass. When they sense hostility, they hide in the grass."),
    ("Sawsbuck", "Season Pokémon", "Normal", "Grass", "They migrate according to the seasons. People can tell the season by looking at Sawsbuck’s horns."),
    ("Emolga", "Sky Squirrel Pokémon", "Electric", "Flying", "The energy made in its cheeks’ electric pouches is stored inside its membrane and released while it is gliding."),
    ("Karrablast", "Clamping Pokémon", "Bug", "", "These mysterious Pokémon evolve when they receive electrical stimulation while they are in the same place as Shelmet."),
    ("Escavalier", "Cavalry Pokémon", "Bug", "Steel", "They fly around at high speed, striking with their pointed spears. Even when in trouble, they face opponents bravely."),
    ("Foongus", "Mushroom Pokémon", "Grass", "Poison", "It lures people in with its Poké Ball pattern, then releases poison spores. Why it resembles a Poké Ball is unknown."),
    ("Amoonguss", "Mushroom Pokémon", "Grass", "Poison", "It lures prey close by dancing and waving its arm caps, which resemble Poké Balls, in a swaying motion."),
    ("Frillish", "Floating Pokémon", "Water", "Ghost", "With its thin, veil-like arms wrapped around the body of its opponent, it sinks to the ocean floor."),
    ("Jellicent", "Floating Pokémon", "Water", "Ghost", "The fate of the ships and crew that wander into Jellicent’s habitat: all sunken, all lost, all vanished."),
    ("Alomomola", "Caring Pokémon", "Water", "", "The special membrane enveloping Alomomola has the ability to heal wounds."),
    ("Joltik", "Attaching Pokémon", "Bug", "Electric", "Joltik that live in cities have learned a technique for sucking electricity from the outlets in houses."),
    ("Galvantula", "EleSpider Pokémon", "Bug", "Electric", "When attacked, they create an electric barrier by spitting out many electrically charged threads."),
    ("Ferroseed", "Thorn Seed Pokémon", "Grass", "Steel", "When threatened, it attacks by shooting a barrage of spikes, which gives it a chance to escape by rolling away."),
    ("Ferrothorn", "Thorn Pod Pokémon", "Grass", "Steel", "It fights by swinging around its three spiky feelers. A hit from these steel spikes can reduce a boulder to rubble."),
    ("Klink", "Gear Pokémon", "Steel", "", "The two minigears that mesh together are predetermined. Each will rebound from other minigears without meshing."),
    ("Klang", "Gear Pokémon", "Steel", "", "By changing the direction in which it rotates, it communicates its feelings to others. When angry, it rotates faster."),
    ("Klinklang", "Gear Pokémon", "Steel", "", "Its red core functions as an energy tank. It fires the charged energy through its spikes into an area."),
    ("Tynamo", "EleFish Pokémon", "Electric", "", "While one alone doesn’t have much power, a chain of many Tynamo can be as powerful as lightning."),
    ("Eelektrik", "EleFish Pokémon", "Electric", "", "They coil around foes and shock them with electricity-generating organs that seem simply to be circular patterns."),
    ("Eelektross", "EleFish Pokémon", "Electric", "", "They crawl out of the ocean using their arms. They will attack prey on shore and immediately drag it into the ocean."),
    ("Elgyem", "Cerebral Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "It uses its strong psychic power to squeeze its opponent’s brain, causing unendurable headaches."),
    ("Beheeyem", "Cerebral Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "It can manipulate an opponent’s memory. Apparently, it communicates by flashing its three different-colored fingers."),
    ("Litwick", "Candle Pokémon", "Ghost", "Fire", "Litwick shines a light that absorbs the life energy of people and Pokémon, which becomes the fuel that it burns."),
    ("Lampent", "Lamp Pokémon", "Ghost", "Fire", "This ominous Pokémon is feared. Through cities it wanders, searching for the spirits of the fallen."),
    ("Chandelure", "Luring Pokémon", "Ghost", "Fire", "It absorbs a spirit, which it then burns. By waving the flames on its arms, it puts its foes into a hypnotic trance."),
    ("Axew", "Tusk Pokémon", "Dragon", "", "They use their tusks to crush the berries they eat. Repeated regrowth makes their tusks strong and sharp."),
    ("Fraxure", "Axe Jaw Pokémon", "Dragon", "", "Since a broken tusk will not grow back, they diligently sharpen their tusks on river rocks after they’ve been fighting."),
    ("Haxorus", "Axe Jaw Pokémon", "Dragon", "", "They are kind but can be relentless when defending territory. They challenge foes with tusks that can cut steel."),
    ("Cubchoo", "Chill Pokémon", "Ice", "", "When it is not feeling well, its mucus gets watery and the power of its Ice-type moves decreases."),
    ("Beartic", "Freezing Pokémon", "Ice", "", "It can make its breath freeze at will. Very able in the water, it swims around in northern seas and catches prey."),
    ("Cryogonal", "Crystallizing Pokémon", "Ice", "", "When its body temperature goes up, it turns into steam and vanishes. When its temperature lowers, it returns to ice."),
    ("Shelmet", "Snail Pokémon", "Bug", "", "When attacked, it defends itself by closing the lid of its shell. It can spit a sticky, poisonous liquid."),
    ("Accelgor", "Shell Out Pokémon", "Bug", "", "When its body dries out, it weakens. So, to prevent dehydration, it wraps itself in many layers of thin membrane."),
    ("Stunfisk", "Trap Pokémon", "Ground", "Electric", "Its skin is very hard, so it is unhurt even if stepped on by sumo wrestlers. It smiles when transmitting electricity."),
    ("Mienfoo", "Martial Arts Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "In fights, they dominate with onslaughts of flowing, continuous attacks. With their sharp claws, they cut enemies."),
    ("Mienshao", "Martial Arts Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "It wields the fur on its arms like a whip. Its arm attacks come with such rapidity that they cannot even be seen."),
    ("Druddigon", "Cave Pokémon", "Dragon", "", "It warms its body by absorbing sunlight with its wings. When its body temperature falls, it can no longer move."),
    ("Golett", "Automaton Pokémon", "Ground", "Ghost", "The energy that burns inside it enables it to move, but no one has yet been able to identify this energy."),
    ("Golurk", "Automaton Pokémon", "Ground", "Ghost", "It flies across the sky at Mach speeds. Removing the seal on its chest makes its internal energy go out of control."),
    ("Pawniard", "Sharp Blade Pokémon", "Dark", "Steel", "Blades comprise this Pokémon’s entire body. If battling dulls the blades, it sharpens them on stones by the river."),
    ("Bisharp", "Sword Blade Pokémon", "Dark", "Steel", "It leads a group of Pawniard. It battles to become the boss, but will be driven from the group if it loses."),
    ("Bouffalant", "Bash Buffalo Pokémon", "Normal", "", "Their fluffy fur absorbs damage, even if they strike foes with a fierce headbutt."),
    ("Rufflet", "Eaglet Pokémon", "Normal", "Flying", "They crush berries with their talons. They bravely stand up to any opponent, no matter how strong it is."),
    ("Braviary", "Valiant Pokémon", "Normal", "Flying", "They fight for their friends without any thought about danger to themselves. One can carry a car while flying."),
    ("Vullaby", "Diapered Pokémon", "Dark", "Flying", "Its wings are too tiny to allow it to fly. As the time approaches for it to evolve, it discards the bones it was wearing."),
    ("Mandibuzz", "Bone Vulture Pokémon", "Dark", "Flying", "It makes a nest out of bones it finds. It grabs weakened prey in its talons and hauls it to its nest of bones."),
    ("Heatmor", "Anteater Pokémon", "Fire", "", "It breathes through a hole in its tail while it burns with an internal fire. Durant is its prey."),
    ("Durant", "Iron Ant Pokémon", "Bug", "Steel", "They attack in groups, covering themselves in steel armor to protect themselves from Heatmor."),
    ("Deino", "Irate Pokémon", "Dark", "Dragon", "It tends to bite everything, and it is not a picky eater. Approaching it carelessly is dangerous."),
    ("Zweilous", "Hostile Pokémon", "Dark", "Dragon", "After it has eaten up all the food in its territory, it moves to another area. Its two heads do not get along."),
    ("Hydreigon", "Brutal Pokémon", "Dark", "Dragon", "This brutal Pokémon travels the skies on its six wings. Anything that moves seems like a foe to it, triggering its attack."),
    ("Larvesta", "Torch Pokémon", "Bug", "Fire", "This Pokémon was believed to have been born from the sun. When it evolves, its entire body is engulfed in flames."),
    ("Volcarona", "Sun Pokémon", "Bug", "Fire", "When volcanic ash darkened the atmosphere, it is said that Volcarona’s fire provided a replacement for the sun."),
    ("Cobalion", "Iron Will Pokémon", "Steel", "Fighting", "This legendary Pokémon battled against humans to protect Pokémon. Its personality is calm and composed."),
    ("Terrakion", "Cavern Pokémon", "Rock", "Fighting", "This Pokémon came to the defense of Pokémon that had lost their homes in a war among humans."),
    ("Virizion", "Grassland Pokémon", "Grass", "Fighting", "This Pokémon fought humans in order to protect its friends. Legends about it continue to be passed down."),
    ("Tornadus", "Cyclone Pokémon", "Flying", "", "The lower half of its body is wrapped in a cloud of energy. It zooms through the sky at 200 mph."),
    ("Thundurus", "Bolt Strike Pokémon", "Electric", "Flying", "Countless charred remains mar the landscape of places through which Thundurus has passed."),
    ("Reshiram", "Vast White Pokémon", "Dragon", "Fire", "This Pokémon appears in legends. It sends flames into the air from its tail, burning up everything around it."),
    ("Zekrom", "Deep Black Pokémon", "Dragon", "Electric", "Concealing itself in lightning clouds, it flies throughout the Unova region. It creates electricity in its tail."),
    ("Landorus", "Abundance Pokémon", "Ground", "Flying", "Lands visited by Landorus grant such bountiful crops that it has been hailed as “The Guardian of the Fields.”"),
    ("Kyurem", "Boundary Pokémon", "Dragon", "Ice", "It generates a powerful, freezing energy inside itself, but its body became frozen when the energy leaked out."),
    ("Keldeo", "Colt Pokémon", "Water", "Fighting", "By blasting water from its hooves, it can glide across water. It excels at using leg moves while battling."),
    ("Meloetta", "Melody Pokémon", "Normal", "Psychic", "Its melodies are sung with a special vocalization method that can control the feelings of those who hear it."),
    ("Genesect", "Paleozoic Pokémon", "Bug", "Steel", "Over 300 million years ago, it was feared as the strongest of hunters. It has been modified by Team Plasma."),
    ("Chespin", "Spiny Nut Pokémon", "Grass", "", "The quills on its head are usually soft. When it flexes them, the points become so hard and sharp that they can pierce rock."),
    ("Quilladin", "Spiny Armor Pokémon", "Grass", "", "It relies on its sturdy shell to deflect predators’ attacks. It counterattacks with its sharp quills."),
    ("Chesnaught", "Spiny Armor Pokémon", "Grass", "Fighting", "Its Tackle is forceful enough to flip a 50-ton tank. It shields its allies from danger with its own body."),
    ("Fennekin", "Fox Pokémon", "Fire", "", "Eating a twig fills it with energy, and its roomy ears give vent to air hotter than 390 degrees Fahrenheit."),
    ("Braixen", "Fox Pokémon", "Fire", "", "It has a twig stuck in its tail. With friction from its tail fur, it sets the twig on fire and launches into battle."),
    ("Delphox", "Fox Pokémon", "Fire", "Psychic", "It gazes into the flame at the tip of its branch to achieve a focused state, which allows it to see into the future."),
    ("Froakie", "Bubble Frog Pokémon", "Water", "", "It secretes flexible bubbles from its chest and back. The bubbles reduce the damage it would otherwise take when attacked."),
    ("Frogadier", "Bubble Frog Pokémon", "Water", "", "It can throw bubble-covered pebbles with precise control, hitting empty cans up to a hundred feet away."),
    ("Greninja", "Ninja Pokémon", "Water", "Dark", "It creates throwing stars out of compressed water. When it spins them and throws them at high speed, these stars can split metal in two."),
    ("Bunnelby", "Digging Pokémon", "Normal", "", "They use their large ears to dig burrows. They will dig the whole night through."),
    ("Diggersby", "Digging Pokémon", "Normal", "Ground", "With their powerful ears, they can heft boulders of a ton or more with ease. They can be a big help at construction sites."),
    ("Fletchling", "Tiny Robin Pokémon", "Normal", "Flying", "These friendly Pokémon send signals to one another with beautiful chirps and tail-feather movements."),
    ("Fletchinder", "Ember Pokémon", "Fire", "Flying", "From its beak, it expels embers that set the tall grass on fire. Then it pounces on the bewildered prey that pop out of the grass."),
    ("Talonflame", "Scorching Pokémon", "Fire", "Flying", "In the fever of an exciting battle, it showers embers from the gaps between its feathers and takes to the air."),
    ("Scatterbug", "Scatterdust Pokémon", "Bug", "", "When under attack from bird Pokémon, it spews a poisonous black powder that causes paralysis on contact."),
    ("Spewpa", "Scatterdust Pokémon", "Bug", "", "It lives hidden within thicket shadows. When predators attack, it quickly bristles the fur covering its body in an effort to threaten them."),
    ("Vivillon", "Scale Pokémon", "Bug", "Flying", "Vivillon with many different patterns are found all over the world. These patterns are affected by the climate of their habitat."),
    ("Litleo", "Lion Cub Pokémon", "Fire", "Normal", "The stronger the opponent it faces, the more heat surges from its mane and the more power flows through its body."),
    ("Pyroar", "Royal Pokémon", "Fire", "Normal", "The male with the largest mane of fire is the leader of the pride."),
    ("Flabébé", "Single Bloom Pokémon", "Fairy", "", "It draws out and controls the hidden power of flowers. The flower Flabébé holds is most likely part of its body."),
    ("Floette", "Single Bloom Pokémon", "Fairy", "", "It flutters around fields of flowers and cares for flowers that are starting to wilt. It draws out the hidden power of flowers to battle."),
    ("Florges", "Garden Pokémon", "Fairy", "", "It claims exquisite flower gardens as its territory, and it obtains power from basking in the energy emitted by flowering plants."),
    ("Skiddo", "Mount Pokémon", "Grass", "", "Thought to be one of the first Pokémon to live in harmony with humans, it has a placid disposition."),
    ("Gogoat", "Mount Pokémon", "Grass", "", "It can tell how its Trainer is feeling by subtle shifts in the grip on its horns. This empathic sense lets them run as if one being."),
    ("Pancham", "Playful Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "It does its best to be taken seriously by its enemies, but its glare is not sufficiently intimidating. Chewing on a leaf is its trademark."),
    ("Pangoro", "Daunting Pokémon", "Fighting", "Dark", "Although it possesses a violent temperament, it won’t put up with bullying. It uses the leaf in its mouth to sense the movements of its enemies."),
    ("Furfrou", "Poodle Pokémon", "Normal", "", "Trimming its fluffy fur not only makes it more elegant but also increases the swiftness of its movements."),
    ("Espurr", "Restraint Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "The organ that emits its intense psychic power is sheltered by its ears to keep power from leaking out."),
    ("Meowstic", "Constraint Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "When in danger, it raises its ears and releases enough psychic power to grind a 10-ton truck into dust."),
    ("Honedge", "Sword Pokémon", "Steel", "Ghost", "Apparently this Pokémon is born when a departed spirit inhabits a sword. It attaches itself to people and drinks their life force."),
    ("Doublade", "Sword Pokémon", "Steel", "Ghost", "When Honedge evolves, it divides into two swords, which cooperate via telepathy to coordinate attacks and slash their enemies to ribbons."),
    ("Aegislash", "Royal Sword Pokémon", "Steel", "Ghost", "Generations of kings were attended by these Pokémon, which used their spectral power to manipulate and control people and Pokémon."),
    ("Spritzee", "Perfume Pokémon", "Fairy", "", "It emits a scent that enraptures those who smell it. This fragrance changes depending on what it has eaten."),
    ("Aromatisse", "Fragrance Pokémon", "Fairy", "", "It devises various scents, pleasant and unpleasant, and emits scents that its enemies dislike in order to gain an edge in battle."),
    ("Swirlix", "Cotton Candy Pokémon", "Fairy", "", "To entangle its opponents in battle, it extrudes white threads as sweet and sticky as cotton candy."),
    ("Slurpuff", "Meringue Pokémon", "Fairy", "", "It can distinguish the faintest of scents. It puts its sensitive sense of smell to use by helping pastry chefs in their work."),
    ("Inkay", "Revolving Pokémon", "Dark", "Psychic", "Opponents who stare at the flashing of the light-emitting spots on its body become dazed and lose their will to fight."),
    ("Malamar", "Overturning Pokémon", "Dark", "Psychic", "It wields the most compelling hypnotic powers of any Pokémon, and it forces others to do whatever it wants."),
    ("Binacle", "Two-Handed Pokémon", "Rock", "Water", "Two Binacle live together on one rock. When they fight, one of them will move to a different rock."),
    ("Barbaracle", "Collective Pokémon", "Rock", "Water", "When they evolve, two Binacle multiply into seven. They fight with the power of seven Binacle."),
    ("Skrelp", "Mock Kelp Pokémon", "Poison", "Water", "Camouflaged as rotten kelp, they spray liquid poison on prey that approaches unawares and then finish it off."),
    ("Dragalge", "Mock Kelp Pokémon", "Poison", "Dragon", "Their poison is strong enough to eat through the hull of a tanker, and they spit it indiscriminately at anything that enters their territory."),
    ("Clauncher", "Water Gun Pokémon", "Water", "", "They knock down flying prey by firing compressed water from their massive claws like shooting a pistol."),
    ("Clawitzer", "Howitzer Pokémon", "Water", "", "Their enormous claws launch cannonballs of water powerful enough to pierce tanker hulls."),
    ("Helioptile", "Generator Pokémon", "Electric", "Normal", "They make their home in deserts. They can generate their energy from basking in the sun, so eating food is not a requirement."),
    ("Heliolisk", "Generator Pokémon", "Electric", "Normal", "They flare their frills and generate energy. A single Heliolisk can generate sufficient electricity to power a skyscraper."),
    ("Tyrunt", "Royal Heir Pokémon", "Rock", "Dragon", "This Pokémon was restored from a fossil. If something happens that it doesn’t like, it throws a tantrum and runs wild."),
    ("Tyrantrum", "Despot Pokémon", "Rock", "Dragon", "Thanks to its gargantuan jaws, which could shred thick metal plates as if they were paper, it was invincible in the ancient world it once inhabited."),
    ("Amaura", "Tundra Pokémon", "Rock", "Ice", "This ancient Pokémon was restored from part of its body that had been frozen in ice for over 100 million years."),
    ("Aurorus", "Tundra Pokémon", "Rock", "Ice", "The diamond-shaped crystals on its body expel air as cold as -240 degrees Fahrenheit, surrounding its enemies and encasing them in ice."),
    ("Sylveon", "Intertwining Pokémon", "Fairy", "", "It sends a soothing aura from its ribbonlike feelers to calm fights."),
    ("Hawlucha", "Wrestling Pokémon", "Fighting", "Flying", "Although its body is small, its proficient fighting skills enable it to keep up with big bruisers like Machamp and Hariyama."),
    ("Dedenne", "Antenna Pokémon", "Electric", "Fairy", "Its whiskers serve as antennas. By sending and receiving electrical waves, it can communicate with others over vast distances."),
    ("Carbink", "Jewel Pokémon", "Rock", "Fairy", "Born from the temperatures and pressures deep underground, it fires beams from the stone in its head."),
    ("Goomy", "Soft Tissue Pokémon", "Dragon", "", "The weakest Dragon-type Pokémon, it lives in damp, shady places, so its body doesn’t dry out."),
    ("Sliggoo", "Soft Tissue Pokémon", "Dragon", "", "It drives away opponents by excreting a sticky liquid that can dissolve anything. Its eyes devolved, so it can’t see anything."),
    ("Goodra", "Dragon Pokémon", "Dragon", "", "This very friendly Dragon-type Pokémon will hug its beloved Trainer, leaving that Trainer covered in sticky slime."),
    ("Klefki", "Key Ring Pokémon", "Steel", "Fairy", "These key collectors threaten any attackers by fiercely jingling their keys at them."),
    ("Phantump", "Stump Pokémon", "Ghost", "Grass", "These Pokémon are created when spirits possess rotten tree stumps. They prefer to live in abandoned forests."),
    ("Trevenant", "Elder Tree Pokémon", "Ghost", "Grass", "It can control trees at will. It will trap people who harm the forest, so they can never leave."),
    ("Pumpkaboo", "Pumpkin Pokémon", "Ghost", "Grass", "The pumpkin body is inhabited by a spirit trapped in this world. As the sun sets, it becomes restless and active."),
    ("Gourgeist", "Pumpkin Pokémon", "Ghost", "Grass", "Singing in eerie voices, they wander town streets on the night of the new moon. Anyone who hears their song is cursed."),
    ("Bergmite", "Ice Chunk Pokémon", "Ice", "", "It blocks opponents’ attacks with the ice that shields its body. It uses cold air to repair any cracks with new ice."),
    ("Avalugg", "Iceberg Pokémon", "Ice", "", "Its ice-covered body is as hard as steel. Its cumbersome frame crushes anything that stands in its way."),
    ("Noibat", "Sound Wave Pokémon", "Flying", "Dragon", "They live in pitch-black caves. Their enormous ears can emit ultrasonic waves of 200,000 hertz."),
    ("Noivern", "Sound Wave Pokémon", "Flying", "Dragon", "They fly around on moonless nights and attack careless prey. Nothing can beat them in a battle in the dark."),
    ("Xerneas", "Life Pokémon", "Fairy", "", "Legends say it can share eternal life. It slept for a thousand years in the form of a tree before its revival."),
    ("Yveltal", "Destruction Pokémon", "Dark", "Flying", "When this legendary Pokémon’s wings and tail feathers spread wide and glow red, it absorbs the life force of living creatures."),
    ("Zygarde", "Order Pokémon", "Dragon", "Ground", "When the Kalos region’s ecosystem falls into disarray, it appears and reveals its secret power."),
    ("Diancie", "Jewel Pokémon", "Rock", "Fairy", "A sudden transformation of Carbink, its pink, glimmering body is said to be the loveliest sight in the whole world."),
    ("Hoopa", "Mischief Pokémon", "Psychic", "Ghost", "This troublemaker sends anything and everything to faraway places using its loop, which can warp space."),
    ("Volcanion", "Steam Pokémon", "Fire", "Water", "It lets out billows of steam and disappears into the dense fog. It’s said to live in mountains where humans do not tread."),
    ("Rowlet", "Grass Quill Pokémon", "Grass", "Flying", "This wary Pokémon uses photosynthesis to store up energy during the day, while becoming active at night."),
    ("Dartrix", "Blade Quill Pokémon", "Grass", "Flying", "A bit of a dandy, it spends its free time preening its wings. Its preoccupation with any dirt on its plumage can leave it unable to battle."),
    ("Decidueye", "Arrow Quill Pokémon", "Grass", "Ghost", "It fires arrow quills from its wings with such precision, they can pierce a pebble at distances over a hundred yards."),
    ("Litten", "Fire Cat Pokémon", "Fire", "", "While grooming itself, it builds up fur inside its stomach. It sets the fur alight and spews fiery attacks, which change based on how it coughs."),
    ("Torracat", "Fire Cat Pokémon", "Fire", "", "At its throat, it bears a bell of fire. The bell rings brightly whenever this Pokémon spits fire."),
    ("Incineroar", "Heel Pokémon", "Fire", "Dark", "This Pokémon has a violent, selfish disposition. If it’s not in the mood to listen, it will ignore its Trainer’s orders with complete nonchalance."),
    ("Popplio", "Sea Lion Pokémon", "Water", "", "This Pokémon snorts body fluids from its nose, blowing balloons to smash into its foes. It’s famous for being a hard worker."),
    ("Brionne", "Pop Star Pokémon", "Water", "", "A skillful dancer, it creates a sequence of water balloons as it dances, and briskly bombards its enemies."),
    ("Primarina", "Soloist Pokémon", "Water", "Fairy", "It controls its water balloons with song. The melody is learned from others of its kind and is passed down from one generation to the next."),
    ("Pikipek", "Woodpecker Pokémon", "Normal", "Flying", "It can peck at a rate of 16 times a second to drill holes in trees. It uses the holes for food storage and for nesting."),
    ("Trumbeak", "Bugle Beak Pokémon", "Normal", "Flying", "It eats berries and stores their seeds in its beak. When it encounters enemies or prey, it fires off all the seeds in a burst."),
    ("Toucannon", "Cannon Pokémon", "Normal", "Flying", "When it battles, its beak heats up. The temperature can easily exceed 212 degrees Fahrenheit, causing severe burns when it hits."),
    ("Yungoos", "Loitering Pokémon", "Normal", "", "With its sharp fangs, it will bite anything. It did not originally live in Alola but was imported from another region."),
    ("Gumshoos", "Stakeout Pokémon", "Normal", "", "When it finds a trace of its prey, it patiently stakes out the location...but it’s always snoozing by nightfall."),
    ("Grubbin", "Larva Pokémon", "Bug", "", "Its strong jaw enables it to scrape trees and slurp out the sap. It normally lives underground."),
    ("Charjabug", "Battery Pokémon", "Bug", "Electric", "Its body is capable of storing electricity. On camping trips, people are grateful to have one around."),
    ("Vikavolt", "Stag Beetle Pokémon", "Bug", "Electric", "It zips around, on sharp lookout for an opening. It concentrates electrical energy within its large jaws and uses it to zap its enemies."),
    ("Crabrawler", "Boxing Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "While guarding its weak points with its pincers, it looks for an opening and unleashes punches. When it loses, it foams at the mouth and faints."),
    ("Crabominable", "Woolly Crab Pokémon", "Fighting", "Ice", "It aimed for the top but got lost and ended up on a snowy mountain. Being forced to endure the cold, this Pokémon evolved and grew fur."),
    ("Oricorio", "Dancing Pokémon", "Fire", "Flying", "It beats its wings together to create fire. As it moves in the steps of its beautiful dance, it bathes opponents in intense flames."),
    ("Cutiefly", "Bee Fly Pokémon", "Bug", "Fairy", "It feeds on the nectar and pollen of flowers. Because it’s able to sense auras, it can identify which flowers are about to bloom."),
    ("Ribombee", "Bee Fly Pokémon", "Bug", "Fairy", "It rolls up pollen into puffs. It makes many different varieties, some used as food and others used in battle."),
    ("Rockruff", "Puppy Pokémon", "Rock", "", "It’s considered to be a good Pokémon for beginners because of its friendliness, but its disposition grows rougher as it grows up."),
    ("Lycanroc", "Wolf Pokémon", "Rock", "", "Its quick movements confuse its enemies. Well equipped with claws and fangs, it also uses the sharp rocks in its mane as weapons."),
    ("Wishiwashi", "Small Fry Pokémon", "Water", "", "When it’s in trouble, its eyes moisten and begin to shine. The shining light attracts its comrades, and they stand together against their enemies."),
    ("Mareanie", "Brutal Star Pokémon", "Poison", "Water", "It plunges the poison spike on its head into its prey. When the prey has weakened, Mareanie deals the finishing blow with its 10 tentacles."),
    ("Toxapex", "Brutal Star Pokémon", "Poison", "Water", "Toxapex crawls along the ocean floor on its 12 legs. It leaves a trail of Corsola bits scattered in its wake."),
    ("Mudbray", "Donkey Pokémon", "Ground", "", "The mud stuck to Mudbray’s hooves enhances its grip and its powerful running gait."),
    ("Mudsdale", "Draft Horse Pokémon", "Ground", "", "It spits a mud that provides resistance to both wind and rain, so the walls of old houses were often coated with it."),
    ("Dewpider", "Water Bubble Pokémon", "Water", "Bug", "It crawls onto the land in search of food. Its water bubble allows it to breathe and protects its soft head."),
    ("Araquanid", "Water Bubble Pokémon", "Water", "Bug", "It delivers headbutts with the water bubble on its head. Small Pokémon get sucked into the bubble, where they drown."),
    ("Fomantis", "Sickle Grass Pokémon", "Grass", "", "During the day, it sleeps and soaks up light. When night falls, it walks around looking for a safer place to sleep."),
    ("Lurantis", "Bloom Sickle Pokémon", "Grass", "", "It requires a lot of effort to maintain Lurantis’s vivid coloring, but some collectors enjoy this work and treat it as their hobby."),
    ("Morelull", "Illuminating Pokémon", "Grass", "Fairy", "It scatters spores that flicker and glow. Anyone seeing these lights falls into a deep slumber."),
    ("Shiinotic", "Illuminating Pokémon", "Grass", "Fairy", "Forests where Shiinotic live are treacherous to enter at night. People confused by its strange lights can never find their way home again."),
    ("Salandit", "Toxic Lizard Pokémon", "Poison", "Fire", "It burns its bodily fluids to create a poisonous gas. When its enemies become disoriented from inhaling the gas, it attacks them."),
    ("Salazzle", "Toxic Lizard Pokémon", "Poison", "Fire", "For some reason, only females have been found. It creates a reverse harem of male Salandit that it lives with."),
    ("Stufful", "Flailing Pokémon", "Normal", "Fighting", "Despite its adorable appearance, when it gets angry and flails about, its arms and legs could knock a pro wrestler sprawling."),
    ("Bewear", "Strong Arm Pokémon", "Normal", "Fighting", "This immensely dangerous Pokémon possesses overwhelming physical strength. Its habitat is generally off-limits."),
    ("Bounsweet", "Fruit Pokémon", "Grass", "", "A delectable aroma pours from its body. They are often swallowed whole by Toucannon lured by that wafting deliciousness."),
    ("Steenee", "Fruit Pokémon", "Grass", "", "The sepals on its head developed to protect its body. These are quite hard, so even if pecked by bird Pokémon, this Pokémon is totally fine."),
    ("Tsareena", "Fruit Pokémon", "Grass", "", "Its long, striking legs aren’t just for show but to be used to kick with skill. In victory, it shows off by kicking the defeated, laughing boisterously."),
    ("Comfey", "Posy Picker Pokémon", "Fairy", "", "It attaches flowers to its highly nutritious vine. This revitalizes the flowers, and they give off an aromatic scent."),
    ("Oranguru", "Sage Pokémon", "Normal", "Psychic", "Known for its extreme intelligence, this Pokémon will look down on inexperienced Trainers, so it’s best suited to veteran Trainers."),
    ("Passimian", "Teamwork Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "They form groups of roughly 20 individuals. Their mutual bond is remarkable—they will never let down a comrade."),
    ("Wimpod", "Turn Tail Pokémon", "Bug", "Water", "This Pokémon is a coward. As it desperately dashes off, the flailing of its many legs leaves a sparkling clean path in its wake."),
    ("Golisopod", "Hard Scale Pokémon", "Bug", "Water", "With a flashing slash of its giant sharp claws, it cleaves seawater—or even air—right in two."),
    ("Sandygast", "Sand Heap Pokémon", "Ghost", "Ground", "Born from a sand mound playfully built by a child, this Pokémon embodies the grudges of the departed."),
    ("Palossand", "Sand Castle Pokémon", "Ghost", "Ground", "Possessed people controlled by this Pokémon transformed its sand mound into a castle. As it evolved, its power to curse grew ever stronger."),
    ("Pyukumuku", "Sea Cucumber Pokémon", "Water", "", "It lives in shallow seas, such as areas near a beach. It can eject its internal organs, which it uses to engulf its prey or battle enemies."),
    ("Type: Null", "Synthetic Pokémon", "Normal", "", "The heavy control mask it wears suppresses its intrinsic capabilities. This Pokémon has some hidden special power."),
    ("Silvally", "Synthetic Pokémon", "Normal", "", "Its trust in its partner is what awakens it. This Pokémon is capable of changing its type, a flexibility that is well displayed in battle."),
    ("Minior", "Meteor Pokémon", "Rock", "Flying", "Originally making its home in the ozone layer, it hurtles to the ground when the shell enclosing its body grows too heavy."),
    ("Komala", "Drowsing Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It is born asleep, and it dies asleep. All its movements are apparently no more than the results of it tossing and turning in its dreams."),
    ("Turtonator", "Blast Turtle Pokémon", "Fire", "Dragon", "The shell on its back is chemically unstable and explodes violently if struck. The hole in its stomach is its weak point."),
    ("Togedemaru", "Roly-Poly Pokémon", "Electric", "Steel", "The spiny fur on its back is normally at rest. When this Pokémon becomes agitated, its fur stands on end and stabs into its attackers."),
    ("Mimikyu", "Disguise Pokémon", "Ghost", "Fairy", "Its actual appearance is unknown. A scholar who saw what was under its rag was overwhelmed by terror and died from the shock."),
    ("Bruxish", "Gnash Teeth Pokémon", "Water", "Psychic", "When it unleashes its psychic power from the protuberance on its head, the grating sound of grinding teeth echoes through the area."),
    ("Drampa", "Placid Pokémon", "Normal", "Dragon", "It has a compassionate personality, but if it is angered, it completely destroys its surroundings with its intense breath."),
    ("Dhelmise", "Sea Creeper Pokémon", "Ghost", "Grass", "Swinging its massive anchor, it can Ko Wailord in a single blow. What appears to be green seaweed is actually its body."),
    ("Jangmo-o", "Scaly Pokémon", "Dragon", "", "It expresses its feelings by smacking its scales. Metallic sounds echo through the tall mountains where Jangmo-o lives."),
    ("Hakamo-o", "Scaly Pokémon", "Dragon", "Fighting", "It leaps at its prey with a courageous shout. Its scaly punches tear its opponents to shreds."),
    ("Kommo-o", "Scaly Pokémon", "Dragon", "Fighting", "When it spots enemies, it threatens them by jingling the scales on its tail. Weak opponents will crack and flee in panic."),
    ("Tapu Koko", "Land Spirit Pokémon", "Electric", "Fairy", "This guardian deity of Melemele is brimming with curiosity. It summons thunderclouds and stores their lightning inside its body."),
    ("Tapu Lele", "Land Spirit Pokémon", "Psychic", "Fairy", "This guardian deity of Akala is guilelessly cruel. The fragrant aroma of flowers is the source of its energy."),
    ("Tapu Bulu", "Land Spirit Pokémon", "Grass", "Fairy", "It pulls large trees up by the roots and swings them around. It causes vegetation to grow, and then it absorbs energy from the growth."),
    ("Tapu Fini", "Land Spirit Pokémon", "Water", "Fairy", "The dense fog it creates brings the downfall and destruction of its confused enemies. Ocean currents are the source of its energy."),
    ("Cosmog", "Nebula Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "Its body is gaseous and frail. It slowly grows as it collects dust from the atmosphere."),
    ("Cosmoem", "Protostar Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "Motionless as if dead, its body is faintly warm to the touch. In the distant past, it was called the cocoon of the stars."),
    ("Solgaleo", "Sunne Pokémon", "Psychic", "Steel", "It is said to live in another world. The intense light it radiates from the surface of its body can make the darkest of nights light up like midday."),
    ("Lunala", "Moone Pokémon", "Psychic", "Ghost", "It is said to be a female evolution of Cosmog. When its third eye activates, away it flies to another world."),
    ("Nihilego", "Parasite Pokémon", "Rock", "Poison", "One of several mysterious Ultra Beasts. People on the street report observing those infested by it suddenly becoming violent."),
    ("Buzzwole", "Swollen Pokémon", "Bug", "Fighting", "This Ultra Beast appeared from another world. It shows off its body, but whether that display is a boast or a threat remains unclear."),
    ("Pheromosa", "Lissome Pokémon", "Bug", "Fighting", "One of the dangerous Ultra Beasts, it has been spotted running across the land at terrific speeds."),
    ("Xurkitree", "Glowing Pokémon", "Electric", "", "One of the mysterious life-forms known as Ultra Beasts. Astonishing electric shocks emanate from its entire body, according to witnesses."),
    ("Celesteela", "Launch Pokémon", "Steel", "Flying", "It appeared from the Ultra Wormhole. Witnesses observed it flying across the sky at high speed."),
    ("Kartana", "Drawn Sword Pokémon", "Grass", "Steel", "This Ultra Beast came from the Ultra Wormhole. It seems not to attack enemies on its own, but its sharp body is a dangerous weapon in itself."),
    ("Guzzlord", "Junkivore Pokémon", "Dark", "Dragon", "It has gobbled mountains and swallowed whole buildings, according to reports. It’s one of the Ultra Beasts."),
    ("Necrozma", "Prism Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "Reminiscent of the Ultra Beasts, this life-form, apparently asleep underground, is thought to have come from another world in ancient times."),
    ("Magearna", "Artificial Pokémon", "Steel", "Fairy", "This artificial Pokémon, constructed more than 500 years ago, can understand human speech but cannot itself speak."),
    ("Marshadow", "Gloomdweller Pokémon", "Fighting", "Ghost", "Able to conceal itself in shadows, it never appears before humans, so its very existence was the stuff of myth."),
    ("Poipole", "Poison Pin Pokémon", "Poison", "", "This Ultra Beast is well enough liked to be chosen as a first partner in its own world."),
    ("Naganadel", "Poison Pin Pokémon", "Poison", "Dragon", "It stores hundreds of liters of poisonous liquid inside its body. It is one of the organisms known as UBs."),
    ("Stakataka", "Rampart Pokémon", "Rock", "Steel", "It appeared from an Ultra Wormhole. Each one appears to be made up of many life-forms stacked one on top of each other."),
    ("Blacephalon", "Fireworks Pokémon", "Fire", "Ghost", "It slithers toward people. Then, without warning, it triggers the explosion of its own head. It’s apparently one kind of Ultra Beast."),
    ("Zeraora", "Thunderclap Pokémon", "Electric", "", "It electrifies its claws and tears its opponents apart with them. Even if they dodge its attack, they’ll be electrocuted by the flying sparks."),
    ("Meltan", "Hex Nut Pokémon", "Steel", "", "It melts particles of iron and other metals found in the subsoil, so it can absorb them into its body of molten steel."),
    ("Melmetal", "Hex Nut Pokémon", "Steel", "", "Revered long ago for its capacity to create iron from nothing, for some reason it has come back to life after 3,000 years."),
    ("Grookey", "Chimp Pokémon", "Grass", "", "When it uses its special stick to strike up a beat, the sound waves produced carry revitalizing energy to the plants and flowers in the area."),
    ("Thwackey", "Beat Pokémon", "Grass", "", "The faster a Thwackey can beat out a rhythm with its two sticks, the more respect it wins from its peers."),
    ("Rillaboom", "Drummer Pokémon", "Grass", "", "By drumming, it taps into the power of its special tree stump. The roots of the stump follow its direction in battle."),
    ("Scorbunny", "Rabbit Pokémon", "Fire", "", "A warm-up of running around gets fire energy coursing through this Pokémon’s body. Once that happens, it’s ready to fight at full power."),
    ("Raboot", "Rabbit Pokémon", "Fire", "", "Its thick and fluffy fur protects it from the cold and enables it to use hotter fire moves."),
    ("Cinderace", "Striker Pokémon", "Fire", "", "It juggles a pebble with its feet, turning it into a burning soccer ball. Its shots strike opponents hard and leave them scorched."),
    ("Sobble", "Water Lizard Pokémon", "Water", "", "When scared, this Pokémon cries. Its tears pack the chemical punch of 100 onions, and attackers won’t be able to resist weeping."),
    ("Drizzile", "Water Lizard Pokémon", "Water", "", "A clever combatant, this Pokémon battles using water balloons created with moisture secreted from its palms."),
    ("Inteleon", "Secret Agent Pokémon", "Water", "", "It has many hidden capabilities, such as fingertips that can shoot water and a membrane on its back that it can use to glide through the air."),
    ("Skwovet", "Cheeky Pokémon", "Normal", "", "Found throughout the Galar region, this Pokémon becomes uneasy if its cheeks are ever completely empty of berries."),
    ("Greedent", "Greedy Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It stashes berries in its tail—so many berries that they fall out constantly. But this Pokémon is a bit slow-witted, so it doesn’t notice the loss."),
    ("Rookidee", "Tiny Bird Pokémon", "Flying", "", "It will bravely challenge any opponent, no matter how powerful. This Pokémon benefits from every battle—even a defeat increases its strength a bit."),
    ("Corvisquire", "Raven Pokémon", "Flying", "", "Smart enough to use tools in battle, these Pokémon have been seen picking up rocks and flinging them or using ropes to wrap up enemies."),
    ("Corviknight", "Raven Pokémon", "Flying", "Steel", "This Pokémon reigns supreme in the skies of the Galar region. The black luster of its steel body could drive terror into the heart of any foe."),
    ("Blipbug", "Larva Pokémon", "Bug", "", "A constant collector of information, this Pokémon is very smart. Very strong is what it isn’t."),
    ("Dottler", "Radome Pokémon", "Bug", "Psychic", "It barely moves, but it’s still alive. Hiding in its shell without food or water seems to have awakened its psychic powers."),
    ("Orbeetle", "Seven Spot Pokémon", "Bug", "Psychic", "It’s famous for its high level of intelligence, and the large size of its brain is proof that it also possesses immense psychic power."),
    ("Nickit", "Fox Pokémon", "Dark", "", "Aided by the soft pads on its feet, it silently raids the food stores of other Pokémon. It survives off its ill-gotten gains."),
    ("Thievul", "Fox Pokémon", "Dark", "", "It secretly marks potential targets with a scent. By following the scent, it stalks its targets and steals from them when they least expect it."),
    ("Gossifleur", "Flowering Pokémon", "Grass", "", "It anchors itself in the ground with its single leg, then basks in the sun. After absorbing enough sunlight, its petals spread as it blooms brilliantly."),
    ("Eldegoss", "Cotton Bloom Pokémon", "Grass", "", "The seeds attached to its cotton fluff are full of nutrients. It spreads them on the wind so that plants and other Pokémon can benefit from them."),
    ("Wooloo", "Sheep Pokémon", "Normal", "", "Its curly fleece is such an effective cushion that this Pokémon could fall off a cliff and stand right back up at the bottom, unharmed."),
    ("Dubwool", "Sheep Pokémon", "Normal", "", "Weave a carpet from its springy wool, and you end up with something closer to a trampoline. You’ll start to bounce the moment you set foot on it."),
    ("Chewtle", "Snapping Pokémon", "Water", "", "Apparently the itch of its teething impels it to snap its jaws at anything in front of it."),
    ("Drednaw", "Bite Pokémon", "Water", "Rock", "With jaws that can shear through steel rods, this highly aggressive Pokémon chomps down on its unfortunate prey."),
    ("Yamper", "Puppy Pokémon", "Electric", "", "This Pokémon is very popular as a herding dog in the Galar region. As it runs, it generates electricity from the base of its tail."),
    ("Boltund", "Dog Pokémon", "Electric", "", "This Pokémon generates electricity and channels it into its legs to keep them going strong. Boltund can run nonstop for three full days."),
    ("Rolycoly", "Coal Pokémon", "Rock", "", "Most of its body has the same composition as coal. Fittingly, this Pokémon was first discovered in coal mines about 400 years ago."),
    ("Carkol", "Coal Pokémon", "Rock", "Fire", "It forms coal inside its body. Coal dropped by this Pokémon once helped fuel the lives of people in the Galar region."),
    ("Coalossal", "Coal Pokémon", "Rock", "Fire", "It’s usually peaceful, but the vandalism of mines enrages it. Offenders will be incinerated with flames that reach 2,700 degrees Fahrenheit."),
    ("Applin", "Apple Core Pokémon", "Grass", "Dragon", "It spends its entire life inside an apple. It hides from its natural enemies, bird Pokémon, by pretending it’s just an apple and nothing more."),
    ("Flapple", "Apple Wing Pokémon", "Grass", "Dragon", "It ate a sour apple, and that induced its evolution. In its cheeks, it stores an acid capable of causing chemical burns."),
    ("Appletun", "Apple Nectar Pokémon", "Grass", "Dragon", "Eating a sweet apple caused its evolution. A nectarous scent wafts from its body, luring in the bug Pokémon it preys on."),
    ("Silicobra", "Sand Snake Pokémon", "Ground", "", "As it digs, it swallows sand and stores it in its neck pouch. The pouch can hold more than 17 pounds of sand."),
    ("Sandaconda", "Sand Snake Pokémon", "Ground", "", "When it contracts its body, over 220 pounds of sand sprays from its nose. If it ever runs out of sand, it becomes disheartened."),
    ("Cramorant", "Gulp Pokémon", "Flying", "Water", "It’s so strong that it can knock out some opponents in a single hit, but it also may forget what it’s battling midfight."),
    ("Arrokuda", "Rush Pokémon", "Water", "", "If it sees any movement around it, this Pokémon charges for it straightaway, leading with its sharply pointed jaw. It’s very proud of that jaw."),
    ("Barraskewda", "Skewer Pokémon", "Water", "", "This Pokémon has a jaw that’s as sharp as a spear and as strong as steel. Apparently Barraskewda’s flesh is surprisingly tasty, too."),
    ("Toxel", "Baby Pokémon", "Electric", "Poison", "It stores poison in an internal poison sac and secretes that poison through its skin. If you touch this Pokémon, a tingling sensation follows."),
    ("Toxtricity", "Punk Pokémon", "Electric", "Poison", "When this Pokémon sounds as if it’s strumming a guitar, it’s actually clawing at the protrusions on its chest to generate electricity."),
    ("Sizzlipede", "Radiator Pokémon", "Fire", "Bug", "It stores flammable gas in its body and uses it to generate heat. The yellow sections on its belly get particularly hot."),
    ("Centiskorch", "Radiator Pokémon", "Fire", "Bug", "When it heats up, its body temperature reaches about 1,500 degrees Fahrenheit. It lashes its body like a whip and launches itself at enemies."),
    ("Clobbopus", "Tantrum Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "It’s very curious, but its means of investigating things is to try to punch them with its tentacles. The search for food is what brings it onto land."),
    ("Grapploct", "Jujitsu Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "A body made up of nothing but muscle makes the grappling moves this Pokémon performs with its tentacles tremendously powerful."),
    ("Sinistea", "Black Tea Pokémon", "Ghost", "", "This Pokémon is said to have been born when a lonely spirit possessed a cold, leftover cup of tea."),
    ("Polteageist", "Black Tea Pokémon", "Ghost", "", "This species lives in antique teapots. Most pots are forgeries, but on rare occasions, an authentic work is found."),
    ("Hatenna", "Calm Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "Via the protrusion on its head, it senses other creatures’ emotions. If you don’t have a calm disposition, it will never warm up to you."),
    ("Hattrem", "Serene Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "No matter who you are, if you bring strong emotions near this Pokémon, it will silence you violently."),
    ("Hatterene", "Silent Pokémon", "Psychic", "Fairy", "It emits psychic power strong enough to cause headaches as a deterrent to the approach of others."),
    ("Impidimp", "Wily Pokémon", "Dark", "Fairy", "Through its nose, it sucks in the emanations produced by people and Pokémon when they feel annoyed. It thrives off this negative energy."),
    ("Morgrem", "Devious Pokémon", "Dark", "Fairy", "When it gets down on all fours as if to beg for forgiveness, it’s trying to lure opponents in so that it can stab them with its spear-like hair."),
    ("Grimmsnarl", "Bulk Up Pokémon", "Dark", "Fairy", "With the hair wrapped around its body helping to enhance its muscles, this Pokémon can overwhelm even Machamp."),
    ("Obstagoon", "Blocking Pokémon", "Dark", "Normal", "Its voice is staggering in volume. Obstagoon has a tendency to take on a threatening posture and shout—this move is known as Obstruct."),
    ("Perrserker", "Viking Pokémon", "Steel", "", "What appears to be an iron helmet is actually hardened hair. This Pokémon lives for the thrill of battle."),
    ("Cursola", "Coral Pokémon", "Ghost", "", "Its shell is overflowing with its heightened otherworldly energy. The ectoplasm serves as protection for this Pokémon’s core spirit."),
    ("Sirfetch’d", "Wild Duck Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "Only Farfetch’d that have survived many battles can attain this evolution. When this Pokémon’s leek withers, it will retire from combat."),
    ("Mr. Rime", "Comedian Pokémon", "Ice", "Psychic", "It’s highly skilled at tap-dancing. It waves its cane of ice in time with its graceful movements."),
    ("Runerigus", "Grudge Pokémon", "Ground", "Ghost", "A powerful curse was woven into an ancient painting. After absorbing the spirit of a Yamask, the painting began to move."),
    ("Milcery", "Cream Pokémon", "Fairy", "", "This Pokémon was born from sweet-smelling particles in the air. Its body is made of cream."),
    ("Alcremie", "Cream Pokémon", "Fairy", "", "When it trusts a Trainer, it will treat them to berries it’s decorated with cream."),
    ("Falinks", "Formation Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "Five of them are troopers, and one is the brass. The brass’s orders are absolute."),
    ("Pincurchin", "Sea Urchin Pokémon", "Electric", "", "It feeds on seaweed, using its teeth to scrape it off rocks. Electric current flows from the tips of its spines."),
    ("Snom", "Worm Pokémon", "Ice", "Bug", "It spits out thread imbued with a frigid sort of energy and uses it to tie its body to branches, disguising itself as an icicle while it sleeps."),
    ("Frosmoth", "Frost Moth Pokémon", "Ice", "Bug", "Icy scales fall from its wings like snow as it flies over fields and mountains. The temperature of its wings is less than −290 degrees Fahrenheit."),
    ("Stonjourner", "Big Rock Pokémon", "Rock", "", "It stands in grasslands, watching the sun’s descent from zenith to horizon. This Pokémon has a talent for delivering dynamic kicks."),
    ("Eiscue", "Penguin Pokémon", "Ice", "", "It drifted in on the flow of ocean waters from a frigid place. It keeps its head iced constantly to make sure it stays nice and cold."),
    ("Indeedee", "Emotion Pokémon", "Psychic", "Normal", "It uses the horns on its head to sense the emotions of others. Males will act as valets for those they serve, looking after their every need."),
    ("Morpeko", "Two-Sided Pokémon", "Electric", "Dark", "As it eats the seeds stored up in its pocket-like pouches, this Pokémon is not just satisfying its constant hunger. It’s also generating electricity."),
    ("Cufant", "Copperderm Pokémon", "Steel", "", "It digs up the ground with its trunk. It’s also very strong, being able to carry loads of over five tons without any problem at all."),
    ("Copperajah", "Copperderm Pokémon", "Steel", "", "They came over from another region long ago and worked together with humans. Their green skin is resistant to water."),
    ("Dracozolt", "Fossil Pokémon", "Electric", "Dragon", "In ancient times, it was unbeatable thanks to its powerful lower body, but it went extinct anyway after it depleted all its plant-based food sources."),
    ("Arctozolt", "Fossil Pokémon", "Electric", "Ice", "The shaking of its freezing upper half is what generates its electricity. It has a hard time walking around."),
    ("Dracovish", "Fossil Pokémon", "Water", "Dragon", "Powerful legs and jaws made it the apex predator of its time. Its own overhunting of its prey was what drove it to extinction."),
    ("Arctovish", "Fossil Pokémon", "Water", "Ice", "Though it’s able to capture prey by freezing its surroundings, it has trouble eating the prey afterward because its mouth is on top of its head."),
    ("Duraludon", "Alloy Pokémon", "Steel", "Dragon", "Its body resembles polished metal, and it’s both lightweight and strong. The only drawback is that it rusts easily."),
    ("Dreepy", "Lingering Pokémon", "Dragon", "Ghost", "After being reborn as a ghost Pokémon, Dreepy wanders the areas it used to inhabit back when it was alive in prehistoric seas."),
    ("Drakloak", "Caretaker Pokémon", "Dragon", "Ghost", "It’s capable of flying faster than 120 mph. It battles alongside Dreepy and dotes on them until they successfully evolve."),
    ("Dragapult", "Stealth Pokémon", "Dragon", "Ghost", "When it isn’t battling, it keeps Dreepy in the holes on its horns. Once a fight starts, it launches the Dreepy like supersonic missiles."),
    ("Zacian", "Warrior Pokémon", "Fairy", "", "Known as a legendary hero, this Pokémon absorbs metal particles, transforming them into a weapon it uses to battle."),
    ("Zamazenta", "Warrior Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "In times past, it worked together with a king of the people to save the Galar region. It absorbs metal that it then uses in battle."),
    ("Eternatus", "Gigantic Pokémon", "Poison", "Dragon", "The core on its chest absorbs energy emanating from the lands of the Galar region. This energy is what allows Eternatus to stay active."),
    ("Kubfu", "Wushu Pokémon", "Fighting", "", "Kubfu trains hard to perfect its moves. The moves it masters will determine which form it takes when it evolves."),
    ("Urshifu", "Wushu Pokémon", "Fighting", "Dark", "This form of Urshifu is a strong believer in the one-hit Ko. Its strategy is to leap in close to foes and land a devastating blow with a hardened fist."),
    ("Zarude", "Rogue Monkey Pokémon", "Dark", "Grass", "Within dense forests, this Pokémon lives in a pack with others of its kind. It’s incredibly aggressive, and the other Pokémon of the forest fear it."),
    ("Regieleki", "Electron Pokémon", "Electric", "", "This Pokémon is a cluster of electrical energy. It’s said that removing the rings on Regieleki’s body will unleash the Pokémon’s latent power."),
    ("Regidrago", "Dragon Orb Pokémon", "Dragon", "", "An academic theory proposes that Regidrago’s arms were once the head of an ancient dragon Pokémon. The theory remains unproven."),
    ("Glastrier", "Wild Horse Pokémon", "Ice", "", "Glastrier emits intense cold from its hooves. It’s also a belligerent Pokémon—anything it wants, it takes by force."),
    ("Spectrier", "Swift Horse Pokémon", "Ghost", "", "It probes its surroundings with all its senses save one—it doesn’t use its sense of sight. Spectrier’s kicks are said to separate soul from body."),
    ("Calyrex", "King Pokémon", "Psychic", "Grass", "Calyrex is a merciful Pokémon, capable of providing healing and blessings. It reigned over the Galar region in times of yore."),
    ("Wyrdeer", "Big Horn Pokémon", "Normal", "Psychic", "The black orbs shine with an uncanny light when the Pokémon is erecting invisible barriers. The fur shed from its beard retains heat well and is a highly useful material for winter clothing."),
    ("Kleavor", "Axe Pokémon", "Bug", "Rock", "A violent creature that fells towering trees with its crude axes and shields itself with hard stone. If one should chance upon this Pokémon in the wilds, one's only recourse is to flee."),
    ("Ursaluna", "Peat Pokémon", "Ground", "Normal", "I believe it was Hisui's swampy terrain that gave Ursaluna its burly physique and newfound capacity to manipulate peat at will."),
    ("Basculegion", "Big Fish Pokémon", "Water", "Ghost", "Clads itself in the souls of comrades that perished before fulfilling their goals of journeying upstream. No other species throughout all Hisui's rivers is Basculegion's equal."),
    ("Sneasler", "Free Climb Pokémon", "Fighting", "Poison", "Because of Sneasler's virulent poison and daunting physical prowess, no other species could hope to best it on the frozen highlands. Preferring solitude, this species does not form packs."),
    ("Overqwil", "Pin Cluster Pokémon", "Dark", "Poison", "Its lancelike spikes and savage temperament have earned it the nickname ”sea fiend.” It slurps up poison to nourish itself."),
    ("Enamorus", "Love-Hate Pokémon", "Fairy", "Flying", "When it flies to this land from across the sea, the bitter winter comes to an end. According to legend, this Pokémon's love gives rise to the budding of fresh life across Hisui."),
    ("Sprigatito", "Grass Cat Pokémon", "Grass", "", "Its fluffy fur is similar in composition to plants. This Pokémon frequently washes its face to keep it from drying out."),
    ("Floragato", "Grass Cat Pokémon", "Grass", "", "Floragato deftly wields the vine hidden beneath its long fur, slamming the hard flower bud against its opponents."),
    ("Meowscarada", "Magician Pokémon", "Grass", "Dark", "This Pokémon uses the reflective fur lining its cape to camouflage the stem of its flower, creating the illusion that the flower is floating."),
    ("Fuecoco", "Fire Croc Pokémon", "Fire", "", "It lies on warm rocks and uses the heat absorbed by its square-shaped scales to create fire energy."),
    ("Crocalor", "Fire Croc Pokémon", "Fire", "", "The combination of Crocalor’s fire energy and overflowing vitality has caused an egg-shaped fireball to appear on the Pokémon’s head."),
    ("Skeledirge", "Singer Pokémon", "Fire", "Ghost", "The fiery bird changes shape when Skeledirge sings. Rumor has it that the bird was born when the fireball on Skeledirge’s head gained a soul."),
    ("Quaxly", "Duckling Pokémon", "Water", "", "This Pokémon migrated to Paldea from distant lands long ago. The gel secreted by its feathers repels water and grime."),
    ("Quaxwell", "Practicing Pokémon", "Water", "", "These Pokémon constantly run through shallow waters to train their legs, then compete with each other to see which of them kicks most gracefully."),
    ("Quaquaval", "Dancer Pokémon", "Water", "Fighting", "A single kick from a Quaquaval can send a truck rolling. This Pokémon uses its powerful legs to perform striking dances from far-off lands."),
    ("Lechonk", "Hog Pokémon", "Normal", "", "It searches for food all day. It possesses a keen sense of smell but doesn’t use it for anything other than foraging."),
    ("Oinkologne", "Hog Pokémon", "Normal", "", "Oinkologne is proud of its fine, glossy skin. It emits a concentrated scent from the tip of its tail."),
    ("Tarountula", "String Ball Pokémon", "Bug", "", "The ball of threads wrapped around its body is elastic enough to deflect the scythes of Scyther, this Pokémon’s natural enemy."),
    ("Spidops", "Trap Pokémon", "Bug", "", "It clings to branches and ceilings using its threads and moves without a sound. It takes out its prey before the prey even notices it."),
    ("Nymble", "Grasshopper Pokémon", "Bug", "", "It has its third set of legs folded up. When it’s in a tough spot, this Pokémon jumps over 30 feet using the strength of its legs."),
    ("Lokix", "Grasshopper Pokémon", "Bug", "Dark", "When it decides to fight all out, it stands on its previously folded legs to enter Showdown Mode. It neutralizes its enemies in short order."),
    ("Pawmi", "Mouse Pokémon", "Electric", "", "It has underdeveloped electric sacs on its cheeks. These sacs can produce electricity only if Pawmi rubs them furiously with the pads on its forepaws."),
    ("Pawmo", "Mouse Pokémon", "Electric", "Fighting", "When its group is attacked, Pawmo is the first to leap into battle, defeating enemies with a fighting technique that utilizes electric shocks."),
    ("Pawmot", "Hands-On Pokémon", "Electric", "Fighting", "This Pokémon normally is slow to react, but once it enters battle, it will strike down its enemies with lightning-fast movements."),
    ("Tandemaus", "Couple Pokémon", "Normal", "", "Exhibiting great teamwork, they use their incisors to cut pieces out of any material that might be useful for a nest, then make off with them."),
    ("Maushold", "Family Pokémon", "Normal", "", "The two little ones just appeared one day. The group might be a family of related Pokémon, but nobody knows for sure."),
    ("Fidough", "Puppy Pokémon", "Fairy", "", "This Pokémon is smooth and moist to the touch. Yeast in Fidough’s breath induces fermentation in the Pokémon’s vicinity."),
    ("Dachsbun", "Dog Pokémon", "Fairy", "", "The pleasant aroma that emanates from this Pokémon’s body helps wheat grow, so Dachsbun has been treasured by farming villages."),
    ("Smoliv", "Olive Pokémon", "Grass", "Normal", "It protects itself from enemies by emitting oil from the fruit on its head. This oil is bitter and astringent enough to make someone flinch."),
    ("Dolliv", "Olive Pokémon", "Grass", "Normal", "Dolliv shares its tasty, fresh-scented oil with others. This species has coexisted with humans since times long gone."),
    ("Arboliva", "Olive Pokémon", "Grass", "Normal", "This calm Pokémon is very compassionate. It will share its delicious, nutrient-rich oil with weakened Pokémon."),
    ("Squawkabilly", "Parrot Pokémon", "Normal", "Flying", "These Pokémon prefer to live in cities. They form flocks based on the color of their feathers, and they fight over territory."),
    ("Nacli", "Rock Salt Pokémon", "Rock", "", "It was born in a layer of rock salt deep under the earth. This species was particularly treasured in the old days, as they would share precious salt."),
    ("Naclstack", "Rock Salt Pokémon", "Rock", "", "This Pokémon dry cures its prey by spraying salt over them. The curing process steals away the water in the prey’s body."),
    ("Garganacl", "Rock Salt Pokémon", "Rock", "", "Garganacl will rub its fingertips together and sprinkle injured Pokémon with salt. Even severe wounds will promptly heal afterward."),
    ("Charcadet", "Fire Child Pokémon", "Fire", "", "Burnt charcoal came to life and became a Pokémon. Possessing a fiery fighting spirit, Charcadet will battle even tough opponents."),
    ("Armarouge", "Fire Warrior Pokémon", "Fire", "Psychic", "Armarouge evolved through the use of a set of armor that belonged to a distinguished warrior. This Pokémon is incredibly loyal."),
    ("Ceruledge", "Fire Blades Pokémon", "Fire", "Ghost", "The fiery blades on its arms burn fiercely with the lingering resentment of a sword wielder who fell before accomplishing their goal."),
    ("Tadbulb", "EleTadpole Pokémon", "Electric", "", "Tadbulb shakes its tail to generate electricity. If it senses danger, it will make its head blink on and off to alert its allies."),
    ("Bellibolt", "EleFrog Pokémon", "Electric", "", "When this Pokémon expands and contracts its wobbly body, the belly-button dynamo in its stomach produces a huge amount of electricity."),
    ("Wattrel", "Storm Petrel Pokémon", "Electric", "Flying", "When its wings catch the wind, the bones within produce electricity. This Pokémon dives into the ocean, catching prey by electrocuting them."),
    ("Kilowattrel", "Frigatebird Pokémon", "Electric", "Flying", "Kilowattrel inflates its throat sac to amplify its electricity. By riding the wind, this Pokémon can fly over 430 miles in a day."),
    ("Maschiff", "Rascal Pokémon", "Dark", "", "It always scowls in an attempt to make opponents take it seriously, but even crying children will burst into laughter when they see Maschiff’s face."),
    ("Mabosstiff", "Boss Pokémon", "Dark", "", "This Pokémon can store energy in its large dewlap. Mabosstiff unleashes this energy all at once to blow away enemies."),
    ("Shroodle", "Toxic Mouse Pokémon", "Poison", "Normal", "Though usually a mellow Pokémon, it will sink its sharp, poison-soaked front teeth into any that anger it, causing paralysis in the object of its ire."),
    ("Grafaiai", "Toxic Monkey Pokémon", "Poison", "Normal", "The color of the poisonous saliva depends on what the Pokémon eats. Grafaiai covers its fingers in its saliva and draws patterns on trees in forests."),
    ("Bramblin", "Tumbleweed Pokémon", "Grass", "Ghost", "A soul unable to move on to the afterlife was blown around by the wind until it got tangled up with dried grass and became a Pokémon."),
    ("Brambleghast", "Tumbleweed Pokémon", "Grass", "Ghost", "It will open the branches of its head to envelop its prey. Once it absorbs all the life energy it needs, it expels the prey and discards it."),
    ("Toedscool", "Woodear Pokémon", "Ground", "Grass", "Toedscool lives in muggy forests. The flaps that fall from its body are chewy and very delicious."),
    ("Toedscruel", "Woodear Pokémon", "Ground", "Grass", "These Pokémon gather into groups and form colonies deep within forests. They absolutely hate it when strangers approach."),
    ("Klawf", "Ambush Pokémon", "Rock", "", "Klawf hangs upside-down from cliffs, waiting for prey. But Klawf can’t remain in this position for long because its blood rushes to its head."),
    ("Capsakid", "Spicy Pepper Pokémon", "Grass", "", "The more sunlight this Pokémon bathes in, the more spicy chemicals are produced by its body, and thus the spicier its moves become."),
    ("Scovillain", "Spicy Pepper Pokémon", "Grass", "Fire", "The red head converts spicy chemicals into fire energy and blasts the surrounding area with a super spicy stream of flame."),
    ("Rellor", "Rolling Pokémon", "Bug", "", "This Pokémon creates a mud ball by mixing sand and dirt with psychic energy. It treasures its mud ball more than its own life."),
    ("Rabsca", "Rolling Pokémon", "Bug", "Psychic", "The body that supports the ball barely moves. Therefore, it is thought that the true body of this Pokémon is actually inside the ball."),
    ("Flittle", "Frill Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "Flittle’s toes levitate about half an inch above the ground because of the psychic power emitted from the frills on the Pokémon’s belly."),
    ("Espathra", "Ostrich Pokémon", "Psychic", "", "It immobilizes opponents by bathing them in psychic power from its large eyes. Despite its appearance, it has a vicious temperament."),
    ("Tinkatink", "Metalsmith Pokémon", "Fairy", "Steel", "It swings its handmade hammer around to protect itself, but the hammer is often stolen by Pokémon that eat metal."),
    ("Tinkatuff", "Hammer Pokémon", "Fairy", "Steel", "This Pokémon will attack groups of Pawniard and Bisharp, gathering metal from them in order to create a large and sturdy hammer."),
    ("Tinkaton", "Hammer Pokémon", "Fairy", "Steel", "This intelligent Pokémon has a very daring disposition. It knocks rocks into the sky with its hammer, aiming for flying Corviknight."),
    ("Wiglett", "Garden Eel Pokémon", "Water", "", "This Pokémon can pick up the scent of a Veluza just over 65 feet away and will hide itself in the sand."),
    ("Wugtrio", "Garden Eel Pokémon", "Water", "", "It has a vicious temperament, contrary to what its appearance may suggest. It wraps its long bodies around prey, then drags the prey into its den."),
    ("Bombirdier", "Item Drop Pokémon", "Flying", "Dark", "It gathers things up in an apron made from shed feathers added to the Pokémon’s chest feathers, then drops those things from high places for fun."),
    ("Finizen", "Dolphin Pokémon", "Water", "", "It likes playing with others of its kind using the water ring on its tail. It uses ultrasonic waves to sense the emotions of other living creatures."),
    ("Palafin", "Dolphin Pokémon", "Water", "", "This Pokémon changes its appearance if it hears its allies calling for help. Palafin will never show anybody its moment of transformation."),
    ("Varoom", "Single-Cyl Pokémon", "Steel", "Poison", "It is said that this Pokémon was born when an unknown poison Pokémon entered and inspirited an engine left at a scrap-processing factory."),
    ("Revavroom", "Multi-Cyl Pokémon", "Steel", "Poison", "It creates a gas out of poison and minerals from rocks. It then detonates the gas in its cylinders—now numbering eight—to generate energy."),
    ("Cyclizar", "Mount Pokémon", "Dragon", "Normal", "Apparently Cyclizar has been allowing people to ride on its back since ancient times. Depictions of this have been found in 10,000-year-old murals."),
    ("Orthworm", "Earthworm Pokémon", "Steel", "", "When attacked, this Pokémon will wield the tendrils on its body like fists and pelt the opponent with a storm of punches."),
    ("Glimmet", "Ore Pokémon", "Rock", "Poison", "It absorbs nutrients from cave walls. The petals it wears are made of crystallized poison."),
    ("Glimmora", "Ore Pokémon", "Rock", "Poison", "When this Pokémon detects danger, it will open up its crystalline petals and fire beams from its conical body."),
    ("Greavard", "Ghost Dog Pokémon", "Ghost", "", "It is said that a dog Pokémon that died in the wild without ever interacting with a human was reborn as this Pokémon."),
    ("Houndstone", "Ghost Dog Pokémon", "Ghost", "", "Houndstone spends most of its time sleeping in graveyards. Among all the dog Pokémon, this one is most loyal to its master."),
    ("Flamigo", "Synchronize Pokémon", "Flying", "Fighting", "This Pokémon apparently ties the base of its neck into a knot so that energy stored in its belly does not escape from its beak."),
    ("Cetoddle", "Terra Whale Pokémon", "Ice", "", "This species left the ocean and began living on land a very long time ago. It seems to be closely related to Wailmer."),
    ("Cetitan", "Terra Whale Pokémon", "Ice", "", "This Pokémon wanders around snowy, icy areas. It protects its body with powerful muscles and a thick layer of fat under its skin."),
    ("Veluza", "Jettison Pokémon", "Water", "Psychic", "When Veluza discards unnecessary flesh, its mind becomes honed and its psychic power increases. The spare flesh has a mild but delicious flavor."),
    ("Dondozo", "Big Catfish Pokémon", "Water", "", "This Pokémon is a glutton, but it’s bad at getting food. It teams up with a Tatsugiri to catch prey."),
    ("Tatsugiri", "Mimicry Pokémon", "Dragon", "Water", "This is a small dragon Pokémon. It lives inside the mouth of Dondozo to protect itself from enemies on the outside."),
    ("Annihilape", "Rage Monkey Pokémon", "Fighting", "Ghost", "When its anger rose beyond a critical point, this Pokémon gained power that is unfettered by the limits of its physical body."),
    ("Clodsire", "Spiny Fish Pokémon", "Poison", "Ground", "When attacked, this Pokémon will retaliate by sticking thick spines out from its body. It’s a risky move that puts everything on the line."),
    ("Farigiraf", "Long Neck Pokémon", "Normal", "Psychic", "Now that the brain waves from the head and tail are synced up, the psychic power of this Pokémon is 10 times stronger than Girafarig’s."),
    ("Dudunsparce", "Land Snake Pokémon", "Normal", "", "This Pokémon uses its hard tail to make its nest by boring holes into bedrock deep underground. The nest can reach lengths of over six miles."),
    ("Kingambit", "Big Blade Pokémon", "Dark", "Steel", "Only a Bisharp that stands above all others in its vast army can evolve into Kingambit."),
    ("Great Tusk", "Paradox Pokémon", "Ground", "Fighting", "Sightings of this Pokémon have occurred in recent years. The name Great Tusk was taken from a creature listed in a certain book."),
    ("Scream Tail", "Paradox Pokémon", "Fairy", "Psychic", "There has been only one reported sighting of this Pokémon. It resembles a mysterious creature depicted in an old expedition journal."),
    ("Brute Bonnet", "Paradox Pokémon", "Grass", "Dark", "It is possible that the creature listed as Brute Bonnet in a certain book could actually be this Pokémon."),
    ("Flutter Mane", "Paradox Pokémon", "Ghost", "Fairy", "This Pokémon has characteristics similar to those of Flutter Mane, a creature mentioned in a certain book."),
    ("Slither Wing", "Paradox Pokémon", "Bug", "Fighting", "This mysterious Pokémon has some similarities to a creature that an old book introduced as Slither Wing."),
    ("Sandy Shocks", "Paradox Pokémon", "Electric", "Ground", "No records exist of this Pokémon being caught. Data is lacking, but the Pokémon’s traits match up with a creature shown in an expedition journal."),
    ("Iron Treads", "Paradox Pokémon", "Ground", "Steel", "This Pokémon closely resembles a scientific weapon that a paranormal magazine claimed was sent to this planet by aliens."),
    ("Iron Bundle", "Paradox Pokémon", "Ice", "Water", "Its shape is similar to a robot featured in a paranormal magazine article. The robot was said to have been created by an ancient civilization."),
    ("Iron Hands", "Paradox Pokémon", "Fighting", "Electric", "It is very similar to a cyborg covered exclusively by a paranormal magazine. The cyborg was said to be the modified form of a certain athlete."),
    ("Iron Jugulis", "Paradox Pokémon", "Dark", "Flying", "It resembles a certain Pokémon introduced in a paranormal magazine, described as the offspring of a Hydreigon that fell in love with a robot."),
    ("Iron Moth", "Paradox Pokémon", "Fire", "Poison", "This Pokémon resembles an unknown object described in a paranormal magazine as a Ufo sent to observe humanity."),
    ("Iron Thorns", "Paradox Pokémon", "Rock", "Electric", "It has some similarities to a Pokémon introduced in a dubious magazine as a Tyranitar from one billion years into the future."),
    ("Frigibax", "Ice Fin Pokémon", "Dragon", "Ice", "Frigibax absorbs heat through its dorsal fin and converts the heat into ice energy. The higher the temperature, the more energy Frigibax stores."),
    ("Arctibax", "Ice Fin Pokémon", "Dragon", "Ice", "Arctibax freezes the air around it, protecting its face with an ice mask and turning its dorsal fin into a blade of ice."),
    ("Baxcalibur", "Ice Dragon Pokémon", "Dragon", "Ice", "This Pokémon blasts cryogenic air out from its mouth. This air can instantly freeze even liquid-hot lava."),
    ("Gimmighoul", "Coin Chest Pokémon", "Ghost", "", "This Pokémon was born inside a treasure chest about 1,500 years ago. It sucks the life-force out of scoundrels who try to steal the treasure."),
    ("Gholdengo", "Coin Entity Pokémon", "Steel", "Ghost", "Its body seems to be made up of 1,000 coins. This Pokémon gets along well with others and is quick to make friends with anybody."),
    ("Wo-Chien", "Ruinous Pokémon", "Dark", "Grass", "The grudge of a person punished for writing the king’s evil deeds upon wooden tablets has clad itself in dead leaves to become a Pokémon."),
    ("Chien-Pao", "Ruinous Pokémon", "Dark", "Ice", "This Pokémon can control 100 tons of fallen snow. It plays around innocently by leaping in and out of avalanches it has caused."),
    ("Ting-Lu", "Ruinous Pokémon", "Dark", "Ground", "The fear poured into an ancient ritual vessel has clad itself in rocks and dirt to become a Pokémon."),
    ("Chi-Yu", "Ruinous Pokémon", "Dark", "Fire", "It controls flames burning at over 5,400 degrees Fahrenheit. It casually swims through the sea of lava it creates by melting rock and sand."),
    ("Roaring Moon", "Paradox Pokémon", "Dragon", "Dark", "It is possible that this is the creature listed as Roaring Moon in an expedition journal that still holds many mysteries."),
    ("Iron Valiant", "Paradox Pokémon", "Fairy", "Fighting", "It has some similarities to a mad scientist’s invention covered in a paranormal magazine."),
    ("Koraidon", "Paradox Pokémon", "Fighting", "Dragon", "This seems to be the Winged King mentioned in an old expedition journal. It was said to have split the land with its bare fists."),
    ("Miraidon", "Paradox Pokémon", "Electric", "Dragon", "Much remains unknown about this creature. It resembles Cyclizar, but it is far more ruthless and powerful."),
    ("Walking Wake", "Paradox Pokémon", "Water", "Dragon", "This ferocious creature is shrouded in mystery. It's named after an aquatic monster mentioned in an old expedition journal."),
    ("Iron Leaves", "Paradox Pokémon", "Grass", "Psychic", "Many of its physical characteristics match those of a Virizion from the future that was covered in a paranormal magazine."),
    ("Dipplin", "Candy Apple Pokémon", "Grass", "Dragon", "Dipplin is two creatures in one Pokémon. Its evolution was triggered by a special apple grown only in one place."),
    ("Poltchageist", "Matcha Pokémon", "Grass", "Ghost", "Supposedly, the regrets of a tea ceremony master who died before perfecting his craft lingered in some matcha and became a Pokémon."),
    ("Sinistcha", "Matcha Pokémon", "Grass", "Ghost", "It pretends to be tea, trying to fool people into drinking it so it can drain their life-force. Its ruse is generally unsuccessful."),
    ("Okidogi", "Retainer Pokémon", "Poison", "Fighting", "After all its muscles were stimulated by the toxic chain around its neck, Okidogi transformed and gained a powerful physique."),
    ("Munkidori", "Retainer Pokémon", "Poison", "Psychic", "The chain is made from toxins that enhance capabilities. It stimulated Munkidori's brain and caused the Pokémon's psychic powers to bloom."),
    ("Fezandipiti", "Retainer Pokémon", "Poison", "Fairy", "Fezandipiti owes its beautiful looks and lovely voice to the toxic stimulants emanating from the chain wrapped around its body."),
    ("Ogerpon", "Mask Pokémon", "Grass", "", "This Pokémon's type changes based on which mask it's wearing. It confounds its enemies with nimble movements and kicks."),
    ("Archaludon", "Alloy Pokémon", "Steel", "Dragon", "It gathers static electricity from its surroundings. The beams it launches when down on all fours are tremendously powerful."),
    ("Hydrapple", "Apple Hydra Pokémon", "Grass", "Dragon", "Seven syrpents live inside an apple made of syrup. The syrpent in the center is the commander."),
    ("Gouging Fire", "Paradox Pokémon", "Fire", "Dragon", "There are scant few reports of this creature being sighted. One short video shows it rampaging and spouting pillars of flame."),
    ("Raging Bolt", "Paradox Pokémon", "Electric", "Dragon", "It's said to incinerate everything around it with lightning launched from its fur. Very little is known about this creature."),
    ("Iron Boulder", "Paradox Pokémon", "Rock", "Psychic", "It resembles a Pokémon described in a dubious magazine as a Terrakion that had been modified by an evil organization."),
    ("Iron Crown", "Paradox Pokémon", "Steel", "Psychic", "It resembles a mysterious object introduced in a paranormal magazine as a cutting-edge weapon shaped like a Cobalion."),
    ("Terapagos", "Tera Pokémon", "Normal", "", "Terapagos protects itself using its power to transform energy into hard crystals. This Pokémon is the source of the Terastal phenomenon."),
    ("Pecharunt", "Subjugation Pokémon", "Poison", "Ghost", "It feeds others toxic mochi that draw out desires and capabilities. Those who eat the mochi fall under Pecharunt’s control, chained to its will."),
  ]
}
